  947                /       THIS IS THE SYSTEM REBOOT ADDRESS.  WHEN ANY PROGRAM EXITS HERE THE DATA FIELD
  948                /       MUST BE 0; THE CONTENTS OF THE AC AND LINK ARE IGNORED.  NOTE: INTERRUPTS
  949                /       SHOULD BE TURNED OFF BECAUSE THE CONTENTS OF 00000-07577 WILL BE LOADED WITH
  950                /       P?S/8 KEYBOARD MONITOR/EDITOR CODE [AND DESIGNATED DATA BUFFERS] WHICH RUNS
  951                /       WITHOUT INTERRUPTS [THUS OVERLAYING ANY POTENTIAL INTERRUPT HANDLER].
  952   
  953   07600* 4240  SBOOT,  JMS     SYSIO                   /BOOT BY CALLING THE HANDLER TO SELF-OVERLAY.
  954   07601* 7600  S7600,  SBOOT                           /CONSTANT 07600; ALSO PROPER READ BUFFER
  955                                                        /VALUE TO CAUSE SELF-OVERLAY.
  956   07602* 0200  S200,   2^100                           /CONSTANT 0200; ALSO USEFUL FUNCTION WORD
  957                                                        /VALUE TO CAUSE SELF-OVERLAY.
  958   07603* 0000          SYSBLK                          /CONSTANT 0000; PROPER BLOCK NUMBER FOR
  959                                                        /SELF-OVERLAY; MUST BE 0000 WHEN BOOTING UP.
  960   
  961                /       ALTHOUGH SEEMINGLY A SUBROUTINE CALL, THERE IS NO ACTUAL RETURN TO THE CALLER.
  962                /       ONCE INITIATED, DATA BREAK TRANSFERS OVERLAY MEMORY; KEY CONTROLLING ADDRESSES
  963                /       AND OTHER PARAMETERS READ IN FROM BLOCK 0000 TAKE CONTROL OF THE OVERALL
  964                /       PROCESS IN MEMORY.  THE ACTUAL TRANSFER IS 07600-03577 [USING ADDRESS
  965                /       WRAP-AROUND KNOWN TO CONTINUE IN FIELD 0].  DESPITE THE READ ARGUMENT 0200 [A
  966                /       CONSTANT NEEDED ELSEWHERE], THE EFFECTIVE FUNCTION ARGUMENT IS TO READ 20
  967                /       [16 DECIMAL] BLOCKS INTO MEMORY.  THE NET EFFECT IS TO READ BLOCKS 0000-0017
  968                /       INTO MEMORY WHICH IS THE INITIAL STEP TOWARDS LOADING THE KEYBOARD MONITOR AND
  969                /       BUILT-IN LINE EDITOR.  [NOTE: FINALIZATION IS PERFORMED WITHIN THE KEYBOARD
  970                /       MONITOR ITSELF.]
  971   
  972                /       ONCE-ONLY CODE WITHIN THE KEYBOARD MONITOR [USUALLY RESIDING IN THE MEMORY
  973                /       LATER USED AS THE COMMAND-LINE BUFFER FOR THE KEYBOARD MONITOR] MOVES THE
  974                /       CONTENTS OF BLOCKS 0015-0017 FROM 03000-03577 TO THE INTENDED ADDRESS RANGE OF
  975                /       07000-07577.  ONCE INITIALIZED, THE MEMORY LAYOUT IS AS FOLLOWS:
  976   
  977                /       BLOCK[S]          MEMORY        FUNCTION
  978   
  979                /         0000          07600-07777     THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER
  980   
  981                /       0001-0014       00000-02777     THE RESIDENT KEYBOARD MONITOR AND LINE EDITOR
  982   
  983                /          N/A          03000-06777     INTERNAL FILE BUFFER FOR THE LINE EDITOR
  984   
  985                /       0015-0016       07000-07377     CACHED COPY OF THE CURRENT UNIT TFS DIRECTORY
  986   
  987                /         0017          07400-07577     THE TRANSIENT AREA OF THE KEYBOARD MONITOR
  988   
  989                /       TRANSIENT AREA DESCRIPTION.
  990   
  991                /       THE TRANSIENT AREA IS USED FOR A VARIETY OF FUNCTIONS USUALLY AVAILABLE WHILE
  992                /       P?S/8 BATCH IS NOT RUNNING.  DURING BATCH OPERATIONS, THE TRANSIENT AREA IS
  993                /       USED AS AN INPUT FILE BUFFER FOR ALL KEYBOARD MONITOR AND LINE EDITOR
  994                /       COMMANDS; AS SUCH, SEVERAL COMMANDS ARE TEMPORARILY INHIBITED DURING BATCH
  995                /       OPERATION.
  996   
  997                /       SINCE BATCH CANNOT PASS CONTROL CHARACTERS BACK TO THE KEYBOARD MONITOR, A FEW
  998                /       INTERNAL FEATURES ARE NOT AVAILABLE DURING BATCH OPERATIONS.  AS SUCH, BATCH
  999                /       OVERLAYS THE CODE SPACE NORMALLY OCCUPIED BY THESE ROUTINES.  A SMALL CHANGE
 1000                /       IS MADE TO THE KEYBOARD MONITOR TO ACCEPT COMMANDS DERIVED FROM THE INPUT FILE
 1001                /       BUFFER CONTENTS [UNPACKED BY BATCH] TO ALLOW MOST NORMAL FUNCTIONALITY.


/    P?S/8 TC01/TC08 SYSTEM HANDLER  P?S PAL V08I    18-AUG-14  PAGE 21

 1003                /       A NOTABLE TEMPORARILY SUPPRESSED COMMAND REQUIRING CONTROL CHARACTER INPUT IS
 1004                /       A SINGLE-LINE MINI-EDITOR FULLY COMPATIBLE WITH FOCAL, 1969 [WITH SEVERAL
 1005                /       ADDED EXTENSIONS UNIQUE TO THE P?S/8 EDITING ENVIRONMENT].  [NOTE: DEPENDING
 1006                /       ON P?S/8 REVISION, THIS COMMAND IS KNOWN AS EITHER THE "EDIT" OR "MODIFY"
 1007                /       COMMAND.]  AUTOMATED FILE EDITING OF COMPLETE LINES OR LINE GROUPS CAN BE
 1008                /       PERFORMED FROM BATCH USING THE ADDITIONAL EDITOR COMMANDS AVAILABLE WITHOUT
 1009                /       RESTRICTION.  BY CLEVER DEPLOYMENT OF LINE EDITOR AND KEYBOARD MONITOR
 1010                /       COMMANDS, A BATCH FILE STREAM CAN SELF-MODIFY TO PRODUCE A VARIETY OF
 1011                /       INTERESTING RESULTS.
 1012   
 1013                /       CERTAIN SYSTEM UTILITIES [FOR EXAMPLE SEARCH AND REPLACE OPERATIONS] ARE
 1014                /       WRITTEN AS AUXILIARY FUNCTIONS OF THE KEYBOARD MONITOR AND WILL LOAD INTO THE
 1015                /       TRANSIENT AREA AS REQUIRED VIA EXECUTION-CLASS COMMANDS.  THE KEYBOARD MONITOR
 1016                /       PROVIDES A SPECIAL EXIT FOR TRANSIENT OVERLAYS USUALLY TAKEN TO RELOAD THE
 1017                /       NORMALLY RESIDENT CODE.  HOWEVER, THIS DOES NOT DETER BATCH OPERATIONS AS ALL
 1018                /       EXECUTION-CLASS COMMANDS ARE SUBJECT TO CHECKPOINT BY BATCH; NORMAL BATCH
 1019                /       PROCESSING CONTINUES AFTER RELOADING THE PROPER BLOCK INTO THE INPUT BUFFER.
 1020   
 1021                /       SINCE THE TFS DIRECTORY AND THE TRANSIENT AREA ARE LOADED ALONG WITH THE
 1022                /       KEYBOARD MONITOR [ALBEIT TO ADDRESSES CONTIGUOUS TO THE KEYBOARD MONITOR AND
 1023                /       NOT THE FINAL MEMORY LOCATIONS], THE SYSTEM LOADS WITH A SINGLE TAPE MOVEMENT
 1024                /       FORWARD.  THE SYSTEM PROMPT WILL BE ISSUED AFTER THE THREE PAGES OF CODE AND
 1025                /       DATA ARE MOVED THROUGH MEMORY TO THEIR INTENDED OPERATING ADDRESSES AS
 1026                /       DESCRIBED ABOVE.  AS SUCH, THE P?S/8 KEYBOARD MONITOR WITH BUILT-IN LINE
 1027                /       EDITOR LOADS IN FAR FASTER THAN MOST OTHER OPERATING SYSTEMS; THIS IS
 1028                /       ESPECIALLY NOTICEABLE ON SYSTEMS BASED ON DECTAPES AND LINCTAPES.
 1029   
 1030                /       RESERVED INTERNAL LOCATIONS.
 1031   
 1032                /       THE FOLLOWING LOCATIONS ARE RESERVED FOR PASSING PARAMETERS TO EXECUTABLE
 1033                /       PROGRAMS AS REQUIRED.  THE EXACT INTERPRETATION OF CERTAIN OF THESE WORDS HAS
 1034                /       EVOLVED OVER TIME; REFER TO PARTICULAR P?S/8 RELEASES FOR EXACT MEANING WHERE
 1035                /       APPLICABLE.
 1036   
 1037                /       OPTION SWITCH WORDS.
 1038   
 1039                /       ALL SYSTEM PROGRAMS CAN REFERENCE THE 36 OPTION SWITCHES "/A" THROUGH "/Z" AND
 1040                /       "/0" THROUGH "/9".  NOTE: COMMAND SPECIFICS MAY OFFER ALTERNATE SYNTAX TO
 1041                /       EXPRESS THESE OPTIONS SUCH AS "(ABC)" WHERE THE RIGHT PARENTHESIS IS OPTIONAL.
 1042                 
 1043                /       NOTE: OPTION BITS ARE ORDERED LEFT TO RIGHT; TWELVE OPTIONS ARE STORED IN EACH
 1044                /       WORD.
 1045   
 1046   07604* 0000  SWAL,   .-.                             /THESE ARE THE PASSED OPTION SWITCHES A-L
 1047   07605* 0000  SWMX,   .-.                             /THESE ARE THE PASSED OPTION SWITCHES M-X
 1048   07606* 0000  SWY9,   .-.                             /THESE ARE THE PASSED OPTION SWITCHES Y-9


