 1050                /       OUTPUT FILE COUNT AND STATUS WORD.
 1051   
 1052                /       THE ORIGINAL R-L MONITOR CAN PASS A MAXIMUM OF 21 [17 DECIMAL] INPUT FILES AND
 1053                /       DOES NOT SUPPORT THE CONCEPT OF DEFINED OUTPUT FILES.  P?S/8 ADDS THE CONCEPT
 1054                /       OF A COUNT OF HOW MANY OF THE PASSED FILES ARE OUTPUT FILES [WHICH ARE ALWAYS
 1055                /       PASSED FIRST IN THE LIST, IF ANY, FOLLOWED BY THE INPUT FILES, IF ANY].
 1056   
 1057                /       ALTHOUGH THE FILE COUNT IS INHERENTLY A QUANTITY THAT CAN BE EXPRESSED IN FIVE
 1058                /       BITS, MOST PROGRAMS DEPEND ON THE HIGH-ORDER SEVEN BITS OF THIS WORD TO BE ALL
 1059                /       ZEROS; THIS WAS THE INITIAL IMPLEMENTATION OF SUPPORT FOR OUTPUT FILES.
 1060   
 1061                /       LATER RELEASES OF P?S/8 REQUIRE PROGRAMS TO MASK OFF THE HIGH-ORDER BITS TO
 1062                /       PRESERVE THE PROPER OUTPUT FILE COUNT.  THE NEWER COMPOSITE MEANING OF THE
 1063                /       WORD IS AS FOLLOWS:
 1064   
 1065                /       BIT[S]  FUNCTION
 1066   
 1067                /       0       IF SET THE P?S/8 SHELL FILE AND COMMUNICATIONS AREA IS VIRTUALIZED
 1068                /               WHEN THE SHELL IS ENABLED.  SEE P?S/8 SHELL DOCUMENTATION FOR MORE
 1069                /               INFORMATION.
 1070   
 1071                /       1-6     SYSTEM DATE GROUP OF EIGHT YEARS; 000000 INDICATES 1900-1907, 001010
 1072                /               INDICATES 1980-1987, 001110 INDICATES 2012-2019; THE LARGEST VALUE OF
 1073                /               111111 INDICATES 2404-2411.  THE LOW-ORDER 12 BITS OF THE DATE ARE
 1074                /               STORED IN "SDATE" [07610].
 1075   
 1076                /       7-11    OUTPUT FILE COUNT IN THE RANGE OF 0000 THROUGH 0021 [17 DECIMAL].
