 1107                /       BITS    MEANING
 1108   
 1109                /       0-2     THE PHYSICAL HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD AVAILABLE.  THIS IS BASED ON DYNAMIC
 1110                /               DISCOVERY AT BOOTUP TIME.  VALUES RANGE FROM 000 FOR A 4K MACHINE TO
 1111                /               111 FOR A 32K MACHINE.  [NOTE: APPENDIX "J" CONTAINS ADDITIONAL
 1112                /               INFORMATION REGARDING ALTERNATE EXTENDED MEMORY SUPPORT FOR CERTAIN
 1113                /               HARDWARE CONFIGURATIONS.]
 1114   
 1115                /       3-5     THE LOGICAL HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD POSSIBLE.  ON MOST CONFIGURATIONS
 1116                /               THIS VALUE IS IDENTICAL TO THE PHYSICAL HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD CONTAINED
 1117                /               IN BITS[0-2] AS DESCRIBED ABOVE; ON CERTAIN SYSTEMS THIS VALUE IS ONE
 1118                /               MEMORY FIELD LOWER DUE TO ONE OR MORE CONFIGURATION ISSUES.  [NOTE:
 1119                /               APPENDIX "J" CONTAINS ADDITIONAL INFORMATION REGARDING CONFIGURATION
 1120                /               SPECIFICS THAT AFFECT THIS VALUE.]
 1121   
 1122                /       6-8     THE LOGICAL HIGHEST FIELD CURRENTLY ALLOWED. POSSIBLE SETTINGS RANGE
 1123                /               FROM 000 THROUGH THE LOGICAL HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD CONTAINED IN
 1124                /               BITS[3-5] AS DESCRIBED ABOVE.  THE P?S/8 "CORE" PROGRAM CAN ADJUST
 1125                /               THE LOGICAL CORE SIZE TO ANY ALLOWED VALUE.
