 1598   07652* 2240          ISZ     SYSIO                   /BUMP TO NEXT.
 1599   
 1600                /       THE SUBROUTINE HEADER NOW POINTS TO THE REQUESTED STARTING BLOCK.  ALL DECTAPE
 1601                /       OPERATIONS MUST SEARCH FOR THIS BLOCK IN THE FORWARD DIRECTION BEFORE READING
 1602                /       OR WRITING [AS INDICATED IN THE FUNCTION WORD].
 1603   
 1604                /       INITIAL SEARCH DIRECTION CONSIDERATIONS.
 1605   
 1606                /       STATISTICALLY, MOST SEARCH OPERATIONS MUST BE INITIATED IN THE REVERSE
 1607                /       DIRECTION FOR ONE OF THE FOLLOWING REASONS:
 1608   
 1609                /       1) SEQUENTIAL TRANSFERS OFTEN INVOLVE PHYSICALLY ADJACENT BLOCKS.  HOWEVER,
 1610                /          SINCE THE PREVIOUS SUBROUTINE CALL STOPPED THE TAPE DRIVE, THE NEXT BLOCK
 1611                /          CANNOT BE DIRECTLY ACCESSED FORWARD; THE TAPE ROLLS WELL PAST THE NEXT
 1612                /          BLOCK DUE TO INERTIA.  THE ONLY WAY TO TRANSFER THE ADJACENT BLOCK IS TO
 1613                /          SEARCH IN REVERSE FOR THE BLOCK TWO HIGHER THAN REQUESTED, THEN TURN THE
 1614                /          TAPE AROUND TO LOCATE THE REQUESTED BLOCK GOING FORWARD. [NOTE: THIS IS THE
 1615                /          BEST POSSIBLE OUTCOME; THE DECTAPE CONTROLLER CAUSES A TWO BLOCK UNDERSHOOT
 1616                /          BEFORE THE REQUESTED BLOCK CAN BE LOCATED WHILE SEARCHING FORWARD.]
 1617   
 1618                /       2) MANY TAPE OPERATIONS NEED TO SEARCH FOR SYSTEM COMPONENTS LOCATED NEAR THE
 1619                /          BEGINNING OF THE TAPE.  THE LATEST REQUESTED BLOCK IS LIKELY MUCH LOWER
 1620                /          THAN THE PRESENT TAPE POSITION.
 1621   
 1622                /       MOST OPERATING SYSTEMS ALWAYS USE REVERSE SEARCH BECAUSE SIMPLISTIC SEARCH
 1623                /       CALCULATION LIMITED TO ALWAYS USING ONE DIRECTION GREATLY FAVORS THE USE OF
 1624                /       INITIAL REVERSE SEARCHES.  HOWEVER, THERE IS ENOUGH CODE SPACE IN THE P?S/8
 1625                /       TC01/TC08 SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER TO CALCULATE FORWARD INITIAL SEARCHES WHEN
 1626                /       BENEFICIAL.  [NOTE: CONTRAST THIS WITH THE CLEARLY INFERIOR METHODOLOGY USED
 1627                /       IN OS/8.  THE CALLING PROGRAM CAN OPTIONALLY SPECIFY A FORWARD SEARCH BY
 1628                /       SETTING BIT[11] OF THE FUNCTION WORD; HOWEVER, AS A PRACTICAL MATTER, THE
 1629                /       CALLING PROGRAM GENERALLY HAS NO BASIS FOR DOING THIS.  THE ENTIRE USAGE OF
 1630                /       THIS FACILITY CONSISTS OF THREE HARD-WIRED CALLS SCATTERED THROUGHOUT OS/8
 1631                /       WHERE THE CERTAINTY OF FORWARD INITIAL SEARCH BEING BENEFICIAL IS KNOWN ON A
 1632                /       STATIC BASIS.  THE ACTUAL OPPORTUNITIES FOR DYNAMIC SEARCH IMPROVEMENT IN ANY
 1633                /       OPERATING SYSTEM ARE FAR GREATER IN NUMBER; THUS, OS/8'S PERFORMANCE IS
 1634                /       NEEDLESSLY INEFFICIENT DUE TO THIS ILL-CONCEIVED IMPLEMENTATION.]


/    P?S/8 TC01/TC08 SYSTEM HANDLER  P?S PAL V08I    18-AUG-14  PAGE 33

 1636                /       CALCULATING THE INITIAL SEARCH DIRECTION.
 1637   
 1638                /       EVERY OPERATION OF THE P?S/8 TC01/TC08 SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER MAINTAINS THE
 1639                /       LAST BLOCK READ OR WRITTEN [INCLUDING THE INITIAL BOOTUP OPERATION, A FAUX
 1640                /       SELF-INITIATED SUBROUTINE CALL].  UPON THE NEXT CALL TO THE DEVICE HANDLER,
 1641                /       THIS VALUE IS USED TO DETERMINE THE OPTIMUM INITIAL SEARCH DIRECTION.
 1642   
 1643                /       AT THIS POINT, THE SUBROUTINE HEADER POINTS TO THE BLOCK NUMBER ARGUMENT.
 1644                /       ONCE THE ENTIRE CALL HAS BEEN PROCESSED, THE HEADER WILL BE INCREMENTED TO
 1645                /       POINT TO THE CALLER'S RETURN ADDRESS.  [NOTE: THROUGHOUT ALL OPERATIONS OF THE
 1646                /       TC01/TC08 DEVICE HANDLER, THE DATA FIELD IS SET TO THE CALLER'S DATA FIELD
 1647                /       ACCORDING TO THE PREVAILING CALLING CONVENTIONS.  LOCAL DATA WITHIN THE
 1648                /       DEVICE HANDLER IS DIRECTLY ADDRESSED.  OTHER DEVICE HANDLERS MAY HAVE MORE
 1649                /       COMPLEX DATA FIELD LOGISTICS REQUIRING RESTORATION OF THE CALLER'S DATA FIELD
 1650                /       ONCE THE DATA FIELD IS CHANGED TO EITHER THE CALLER'S BUFFER FIELD OR THE
 1651                /       EXTENDED DEVICE HANDLER FIELD IF APPLICABLE.]
 1652   
 1653   07653* 1640          TAD I   SYSIO                   /GET THE DESIRED STARTING BLOCK NUMBER.
 1654   07654* 7161          CLL CML CMA IAC                 /INVERT FOR COMPARISON; LINK SET UNLESS 0000.
 1655   07655* 1345  SGETBLK,TAD     SBLK                    /COMPARE TO LATEST BLOCK FROM PREVIOUS CALL.
 1656   07656* 1344          TAD     SOVSHT                  /ADD ON OVERSHOOT FACTOR.
 1657   
 1658                /       THE LINK NOW CONTAINS THE INVERSE OF INTENDED INITIAL SEARCH DIRECTION.
 1659   
 1660                /       LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY MODIFICATIONS.
 1661   
 1662                /       IF THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IS IN EFFECT, THE PREVIOUS TWO INSTRUCTIONS ARE
 1663                /       REPLACED AS FOLLOWS:
 1664   
 1665                /       *SGETBLK                        /OVER "TAD SBLK" INSTRUCTION AND FOLLOWING.
 1666   
 1667                /       CIF     XX                      /WILL BE "CIF" TO THE HIGHEST PHYSICAL FIELD.
 1668                /       JMP     GETSBLK                 /THIS IS ON PAGE ZERO OF THE CONSOLE OVERLAY.
 1669   
 1670                /       THE CONSOLE OVERLAY CODE FOR THE TC01/TC08 DEVICE HANDLER CHANGES THE LOGICAL
 1671                /       FLOW TO REFERENCE THE LATEST BLOCK VALUE ASSOCIATED WITH THE CURRENT LOGICAL
 1672                /       TAPE DRIVE UNIT INSTEAD OF THE SHARED VALUE.  A TABLE OF LATEST BLOCK VALUES
 1673                /       IS MAINTAINED WITHIN THE OVERLAY FOR ALL POSSIBLE TAPE DRIVES.  WHEN THE
 1674                /       DEVICE HANDLER CODE IS REJOINED, THE APPROPRIATE LATEST BLOCK IS ADDED TO THE
 1675                /       AC FOLLOWED BY CAREFULLY ADDING ON THE CUSTOM OVERSHOOT FACTOR.  THIS
 1676                /       ELIMINATES ANY POTENTIAL INITIAL CURRENT BLOCK CALCULATION MISHAPS ASSOCIATED
 1677                /       WITH USING THE SHARED VALUE.
 1678   
 1679                /       INITIAL TC01/TC08 DECTAPE CONTROLLER SETUP.
 1680   
 1681                /       THE TC01/TC08 DECTAPE CONTROLLER TAPE DIRECTION BIT IS SET FOR REVERSE MOTION,
 1682                /       CLEAR FOR FORWARD MOTION.  THE LINK IS SET TO THE INVERSE OF INTENDED SEARCH
 1683                /       DIRECTION.  STATUS REGISTER "A" WILL BE LOADED WITH THE LOGICAL DRIVE UNIT
 1684                /       BITS SET, FUNCTION 010 [NORMAL MODE SEARCH] AND THE INVERSE OF INTENDED
 1685                /       INITIAL SEARCH DIRECTION [TAKEN FROM THE LINK].  THE MOTION AND
 1686                /       INTERRUPT-ENABLE BITS WILL BE CLEAR.  AC[10-11] WILL BE CLEAR TO RESET THE
 1687                /       DECTAPE AND ERROR FLAGS.  AT A LATER TIME, THE MOTION AND DIRECTION BITS WILL
 1688                /       BE SET VIA AN .XOR. OPERATION WITHIN THE GENERAL FLAG WAIT SUBROUTINE.  AS A
 1689                /       RESULT, THE SELECTED TAPE DRIVE UNIT WILL BE SET IN MOTION IN THE INTENDED
 1690                /       DIRECTION.


/    P?S/8 TC01/TC08 SYSTEM HANDLER  P?S PAL V08I    18-AUG-14  PAGE 34

 1692                /       THE LAST TRANSFERRED BLOCK [FROM THE PREVIOUS SUBROUTINE CALL] IS COMPARED TO
 1693                /       THE LATEST REQUESTED BLOCK; AN OVERSHOOT FACTOR IS ADDED TO COMPENSATE FOR
 1694                /       PRESUMED WORST-CASE INERTIAL ROLL. [NOTE: IT MUST BE ASSUMED THE TAPE DRIVE
 1695                /       HAS COASTED TO A COMPLETE STOP AFTER THE PREVIOUS OPERATION WHICH CLEARED THE
 1696                /       CONTROLLER MOTION BIT.  CONTEMPLATING CASES WHERE THE TAPE IS POSSIBLY STILL
 1697                /       IN MOTION CAN LEAD TO INSTANCES OF "SHOESHINE" EFFECT.]
 1698   
 1699                /       SYSTEMS THAT USE TU56 DRIVES EXCLUSIVELY MIGHT ALLOW THE OVERSHOOT FACTOR TO
 1700                /       BE LOWERED BY ONE BLOCK; HOWEVER, AS A PRACTICAL MATTER, LITTLE IS GAINED BY
 1701                /       CHANGING THIS VALUE AS MOST SEQUENTIALLY-ISSUED CALLS ARE EITHER FOR THE NEXT
 1702                /       PHYSICAL BLOCK OR FOR A BLOCK LOCATED SIGNIFICANTLY AWAY FROM THE PRESENT
 1703                /       POSITION.  THE PURPOSE OF THE OVERSHOOT FACTOR IS TO CREATE A DIVIDING LINE
 1704                /       FOR ALL POTENTIAL CIRCUMSTANCES WHERE AN INITIAL FORWARD SEARCH WOULD APPLY.
 1705                /       THIS IS ESTIMATED AT 20 PERCENT OF ALL ACTUAL CALLS FOR TYPICAL SYSTEM USAGE.
 1706   
 1707                /       REPRESENTATIVE INITIAL SEARCH DIRECTION EXAMPLES; FORWARD SEARCH IF LINK SET.
 1708   
 1709                /       PRV. BLOCK   REQ. BLOCK   L
 1710   
 1711                /          0000         0001      0
 1712   
 1713                /          0001         0000      0
 1714   
 1715                /          0000         0000      0
 1716   
 1717                /          0000         0010      0
 1718   
 1719                /          0000         0011      1
 1720   
 1721                /          0000         0012      1
 1722   
 1723                /          2000         2001      0
 1724   
 1725                /          2000         2010      0
 1726   
 1727                /          2000         2011      1
 1728   
 1729                /          2000         2012      1
 1730   
 1731                /          2000         0000      0
 1732   
 1733                /          2000         0001      0
 1734   
 1735                /       ABSOLUTE BLOCKS NUMBERED LESS THAN OR EQUAL TO THE OVERSHOOT FACTOR WILL
 1736                /       RESULT IN AN INITIAL REVERSE SEARCH [INCLUDING BLOCK 0000 WHICH IS PROPERLY
 1737                /       HANDLED] WHEN THE TAPE IS LOCATED NEAR THE REVERSE END ZONE.  INITIAL SEARCH
 1738                /       DIRECTION FOR HIGHER BLOCKS WILL BE FORWARD IF THE REQUESTED BLOCK IS MORE
 1739                /       THAN THE OVERSHOOT FACTOR FORWARD OF THE PRESENT TAPE POSITION.
 1740   
 1741                /       ALL [LINCTAPE OR] DECTAPE-BASED OPERATING SYSTEMS INHERENTLY HAVE SOME
 1742                /       OPPORTUNITIES TO EXPLOIT INITIAL FORWARD SEARCH DIRECTION; DYNAMIC DETECTION
 1743                /       WILL ALWAYS ACHIEVE THIS TO THE FULLEST EXTENT POSSIBLE.
 1744   
 1745                /       APPENDIX "L" ILLUSTRATES A WAY TO TAKE ADVANTAGE OF FORWARD INITIAL SEARCH IN
 1746                /       THE P?S/8 KEYBOARD MONITOR/EDITOR ENVIRONMENT FOR FASTER PROGRAM ASSEMBLY.


