 1751                /       ERROR RECOVERY CONSIDERATIONS.
 1752   
 1753                /       GENERAL ERROR RECOVERY FOR ALL DETECTED ERRORS [EXCEPT END ZONE ERRORS] STARTS
 1754                /       HERE.  THE AC CONTAINS STATUS REGISTER "B" DATA [AND WILL BE CLEARED]; THE
 1755                /       LINK CONTAINS THE MARK ERROR STATUS.  REVERSE INITIAL SEARCH IS RECOMMENDED
 1756                /       FOR MOST RECOVERY SITUATIONS.  IF A FORWARD SEARCH WAS IN PROGRESS WHEN A MARK
 1757                /       ERROR OCCURRED, THE INITIAL SEARCH WILL BE FORWARD.  SINCE MARK ERRORS ARE
 1758                /       [HOPEFULLY] UNLIKELY, YET MOSTLY SEEN DURING SEARCH OPERATIONS, THIS IS A GOOD
 1759                /       OVERALL COMPROMISE.  IN MOST CASES THE TAPE WILL CONTINUE TO MOVE TOWARDS THE
 1760                /       TARGET BLOCK; WHEN THERE ARE MAINTENANCE ISSUES, THIS COULD LEAD TO A SERIES
 1761                /       OF REPEATING MARK ERROR EVENTS.  SITUATIONS LIKE THIS REQUIRE REMEDIATION
 1762                /       BEFORE THE TAPE DEGRADES FURTHER AND THERE IS THE RISK OF PERMANENT DATA LOSS.
 1763                /       IT IS HOPED THAT HAVING TO DEAL WITH THE OBVIOUS SEQUENCE OF REPEAT FAILURES
 1764                /       WILL ALERT THE USER TO THE SERIOUS NATURE OF THE PROBLEM AT HAND BEFORE THE
 1765                /       SITUATION ESCALATES TO MASSIVE RELIABILITY PROBLEMS.
 1766   
