 1844                /       THIS IS THE ENTRY POINT FOR CONTINUING AN ONGOING SEARCH OPERATION.  THE LINK
 1845                /       WILL BE SET TO MAINTAIN THE CURRENT DIRECTION OR CLEAR TO REVERSE DIRECTION.
 1846   
 1847                /       THERE ARE FOUR POSSIBILITIES:
 1848   
 1849                /       1) FORWARD SEARCH IN PROGRESS - THE TAPE IS MOVING FORWARD TOWARDS THE TARGET
 1850                /          BLOCK. THE LINK IS SET TO MAINTAIN FORWARD MOTION.
 1851   
 1852                /       2) REVERSE SEARCH IN PROGRESS - THE TAPE IS MOVING IN THE REVERSE DIRECTION
 1853                /          TOWARDS THE BLOCK TWO HIGHER THAN THE TARGET BLOCK.  THE LINK IS SET TO
 1854                /          MAINTAIN REVERSE MOTION.
 1855   
 1856                /       3) REVERSE SEARCH ENDED - THE TARGET BLOCK PLUS TWO HAS BEEN LOCATED WHILE
 1857                /          MOVING IN THE REVERSE DIRECTION.  THE LINK IS CLEAR; THE TAPE WILL BE
 1858                /          TURNED AROUND.
 1859   
 1860                /       4) FORWARD SEARCH TOO FAR - THE TAPE IS MOVING FORWARD OF THE TARGET BLOCK.
 1861                /          THE LINK IS CLEAR; THE TAPE WILL BE TURNED AROUND. [NOTE: THIS CASE IS NOT
 1862                /          LIKELY TO OCCUR UNLESS THE TAPE IS MANUALLY REPOSITIONED OR THERE WAS AN
 1863                /          ANOMALY INVOLVING DRIVE UNIT CHANGE FROM THAT USED IN THE PREVIOUS CALL.]
