 1949   07715* 6774          DTLB                            /LOAD THE TRANSFER FIELD.  NOTE: CLEARS AC.


/    P?S/8 TC01/TC08 SYSTEM HANDLER  P?S PAL V08I    18-AUG-14  PAGE 39

 1951                /       IN THE ORIGINAL R-L MONITOR SYSTEM, THE PAGE COUNT IS PASSED AS -[NUMBER OF
 1952                /       BLOCKS TO TRANSFER].  IN P?S/8 [AND OS/8 ET AL.] BITS[1-5] OF THE FUNCTION
 1953                /       WORD SERVE THIS PURPOSE; ADDITIONALLY, AN ENTIRE MEMORY FIELD CAN BE SPECIFIED
 1954                /       BY SETTING THESE BITS TO ZERO.  [NOTE: THIS IS MOOT IN THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM
 1955                /       AS EXTENDED MEMORY IS NOT SUPPORTED.]
 1956   
 1957   07716* 1352          TAD     SFUNCT                  /GET THE FUNCTION WORD AGAIN
 1958   07717* 7004          RAL                             /SHIFT LEFT; READ/WRITE BIT TO LINK
 1959   07720* 0201          AND     S7600/(7600)            /ISOLATE PAGE COUNT BITS
 1960   07721* 3351          DCA     SBLKCT                  /STORE FOR COUNTDOWN LATER
 1961   
 1962                /       THE PAGE COUNT SHIFTED LEFT ONE BIT WILL RANGE FROM 0200 FOR A SINGLE PAGE
 1963                /       TRANSFER THROUGH 7600 FOR A 31 PAGE TRANSFER; 0000 INDICATES A 32 PAGE
 1964                /       [ENTIRE MEMORY FIELD] TRANSFER.  THIS VALUE WILL BE COUNTED DOWN BY 200 PER
 1965                /       TRANSFERRED BLOCK UNTIL ALL BLOCKS ARE PROCESSED.
 1966   
 1967                /       DEPENDING ON EXACT CODING REQUIREMENTS, THIS SECTION MIGHT BE REWORKED INTO A
 1968                /       MORE CONVENTIONAL "ISZ" INSTRUCTION COUNTING LOOP SET TO -[NUMBER OF PAGES TO
 1969                /       TRANSFER].  HOWEVER, THE ALL-ZEROS CASE MUST BE PROPERLY DEALT WITH.  THE CODE
 1970                /       ALSO HAS TO PRESERVE THE READ/WRITE BIT IN THE LINK OR PROCESS THAT IN
 1971                /       SEPARATE [AND LONGER] CODE. IT WOULD APPEAR THE CODE USED ABOVE OCCUPIES THE
 1972                /       LEAST OVERALL CODE SPACE INCLUDING THE EASILY OBTAINED CONSTANT 7600. [NOTE:
 1973                /       ALTERNATE METHODS MIGHT REQUIRE ONE OR MORE UNIQUE CONSTANTS AS PART OF THE
 1974                /       COMPLETE IMPLEMENTATION LEADING TO A NET LARGER RESULT.]
 1975   
 1976                /       SETTING THE CONTROLLER FOR DATA TRANSFER.
 1977   
 1978                /       AT THIS POINT THE CONTROLLER MUST BE PUT IN READ MODE OR WRITE MODE AS
 1979                /       DETERMINED BY THE HIGH-ORDER BIT OF THE FUNCTION WORD [CURRENTLY IN THE LINK].
 1980   
 1981                /       STATUS REGISTER "A" UPDATES ARE PERFORMED BY .XOR. TRANSFERS IN THE GENERAL
 1982                /       FLAG WAIT ROUTINE.  THE BITS OF THE AC MUST BE SET AS FOLLOWS:
 1983   
 1984                /       BITS[0-2] MUST BE 000 TO MAINTAIN THE CURRENT UNIT SELECT BITS.
 1985   
 1986                /       BITS[3-4] MUST BE 00 TO MAINTAIN FORWARD TAPE MOTION.
 1987   
 1988                /       BIT[5] MUST BE 0 TO MAINTAIN NORMAL MODE.
 1989   
 1990                /       BITS[6-8] MUST BE SET TO 011 [FOR READ] OR 101 [FOR WRITE].
 1991   
 1992                /       BIT[9] MUST BE 0 TO MAINTAIN CONTROLLER INTERRUPTS OFF.
 1993   
 1994                /       BIT[10] IS ARBITRARY AS THERE ARE NO ERRORS AFTER A SUCCESSFUL SEARCH.
 1995   
 1996                /       BIT[11] MUST BE 0 TO CLEAR THE DECTAPE FLAG.
 1997   
 1998   07722* 7004          RAL                             /MOVE READ/WRITE BIT TO AC[11]
 1999   07723* 7001          IAC                             /0001 IF READING, 0002 IF WRITING
 2000   07724* 7126          CLL CML RTL                     /0006 IF READING, 0012 IF WRITING
 2001   07725* 7006          RTL                             /0030 IF READING, 0050 IF WRITING
 2002   
 2003                /       THE AC IS NOW SET CORRECTLY TO CHANGE OPERATING MODES. [NOTE: SUBSEQUENT CALLS
 2004                /       SHOULD BE MADE WITH THE AC CLEAR TO MAINTAIN THE CURRENT MODE.]


/    P?S/8 TC01/TC08 SYSTEM HANDLER  P?S PAL V08I    18-AUG-14  PAGE 40

 2006   07726* 4212  SBLKLP, JMS     SYSWAIT                 /WAIT FOR A BLOCK TO BE READ OR WRITTEN; THE
 2007                                                        /WORD COUNT REGISTER IS SET TO -200 EACH TIME.
 2008   
 2009                /       NOTE: COMES HERE DURING THE BOOTUP PROCESS AFTER THE DECTAPE FLAG RAISES.
 2010   
 2011   07727* 2345  SBLKRET,ISZ     SBLK                    /BUMP LATEST BLOCK.
 2012   07730* 7320          CLA CLL CML                     /CLEAR STATUS REGISTER "B" JUNK; SET LINK NOW.
 2013   07731* 1351          TAD     SBLKCT                  /GET REMAINING WORD COUNT.
 2014   07732* 1201          TAD     S7600/(-200)            /SUBTRACT 200; WILL CLEAR LINK WHEN 0000.
 2015   07733* 7450          SNA                             /SKIP IF MORE BLOCKS TO PROCESS.
 2016   07734* 5337          JMP     SDONE                   /JUMP IF DONE.
 2017   07735* 3351          DCA     SBLKCT                  /STORE BACK UPDATED VALUE FOR NEXT TIME.
 2018   07736* 5326          JMP     SBLKLP                  /GO TRANSFER ANOTHER BLOCK.
 2019   
 2020                /       COMES HERE TO STOP THE TAPE AFTER ALL BLOCKS ARE TRANSFERRED.
 2021   
 2022                /       NOTE: OVER THE YEARS THIS SECTION HAS BEEN REWRITTEN SEVERAL TIMES.  THE
 2023                /       OVERHEAD ASSOCIATED WITH PRESERVING THE DRIVE UNIT BITS PRECLUDES THE USE OF
 2024                /       THE DTLA OPERATION TO UPDATE STATUS REGISTER "A".  IT IS NOT NECESSARY TO
 2025                /       CHANGE THE CONTROLLER FUNCTION AS LONG AS THE DIRECTION BIT IS MAINTAINED AND
 2026                /       THE MOTION BIT IS CLEARED.  THIS WILL BE IMPLEMENTED USING THE DTXA
 2027                /       INSTRUCTION TO UPDATE STATUS REGISTER "A" BY AN .XOR. OPERATION.
 2028   
 2029                /       ISSUES ASSOCIATED WITH STATUS REGISTER "A" UPDATE ARE AS FOLLOWS:
 2030   
 2031                /       1) AC[0-2] MUST BE ZERO TO PREVENT THE UNIT BITS FROM CHANGING WHEN TURNING
 2032                /          OFF THE MOTION BIT.  UNEXPECTED PROBLEMS OCCUR WHEN CHANGING TOO MANY
 2033                /          BITS AT ONCE.
 2034   
 2035                /       2) AC[3] MUST BE ZERO TO PREVENT TURNING THE TAPE AROUND WHICH CAN LEAD TO
 2036                /          UNEXPECTED PROBLEMS, POSSIBLY AFFECTING THE NEXT HANDLER CALL.
 2037   
 2038                /       3) AC[4] MUST BE SET TO TURN OFF THE MOTION BIT WHILE HOLDING MOST OF THE
 2039                /          OTHER BITS CONSTANT.
 2040   
 2041                /       4) AC[5] IS ARBITRARY AS CONTINUOUS MODE IS IGNORED DURING MOTION COMMANDS.
 2042   
 2043                /       5) AC[6-8] MUST BE 000 TO MAINTAIN THE PREVIOUS [READ OR WRITE] COMMAND.
 2044                /          ALTERNATIVELY, THE COMMAND CAN BE CHANGED TO MOVE [000] WHICH REQUIRES
 2045                /          PRIOR KNOWLEDGE OF BITS[6-8] OF STATUS REGISTER "A".
 2046   
 2047                /       6) AC[9] SHOULD BE ZERO TO AVOID INTERRUPT-RELATED PROBLEMS.
 2048   
 2049                /       7) AC[10] IS ARBITRARY AS THE ERROR FLAG IS KNOWN TO BE CLEAR.
 2050   
 2051                /       8) AC[11] SHOULD BE ZERO TO CLEAR THE DECTAPE FLAG.
 2052   
 2053                /       ALL THINGS CONSIDERED, SETTING THE AC TO 0200 IS THE PREFERRED METHOD. IF
 2054                /       NECESSARY, ALTERNATE VALUES CAN BE CONSTRUCTED HEEDING THE ABOVE.
 2055   
 2056   07737* 1202  SDONE,  TAD     S200/(200)              /SET THE MOTION BIT [TO CLEAR IT].
 2057   07740* 6764          DTXA                            /STOP THE TAPE DRIVE; THE AC IS NOW CLEAR.


