 2340                /       RESTART OPERATION CONSIDERATIONS.
 2341   
 2342                /       WHEN THE BOOTSTRAP CODE IS INITIATED, THE DECTAPE IS REWOUND INTO THE REVERSE
 2343                /       END ZONE.  THE BOOTSTRAP THEN INITIATES A FORWARD READ OPERATION; WHEN
 2344                /       PERFORMED IN THIS MANNER, BLOCK 0000 WILL BE TRANSFERRED INTO MEMORY AS THE
 2345                /       DECTAPE COMES OUT OF THE REVERSE END ZONE.
 2346   
 2347                /       DURING THE TAPE BLOCK DMA TRANSFER, THE CONTENTS OF TAPE BLOCK 0000 GRADUALLY
 2348                /       REPLACES THE CODE DEFINED HERE; THE ONLY REQUIREMENT IS THE REPLACEMENT WAIT
 2349                /       LOOP CODE MUST BE SUFFICIENTLY COMPATIBLE WITH THE BOOTSTRAP-PROVIDED WAIT
 2350                /       LOOP TO ALLOW THE DMA TO COMPLETE PROPERLY [SUBJECT TO POSSIBLE DATA TRANSFER
 2351                /       LENGTH ALTERATION ONCE THE WORD COUNT AND CURRENT ADDRESS LOCATIONS
 2352                /       [07754-07755] ARE OVERLAID BY THE CORRESPONDING DATA ON THE DECTAPE BLOCK].
 2353   
 2354                /       NOTE: CONFORMING WITH THE STANDARD TC01/TC08 BOOTSTRAP CONVENTION REQUIRES THE
 2355                /       LOOP WAITING FOR THE DONE FLAG BE PLACED IN MEMORY LOCATIONS 07616-07617.
 2356   
 2357                /       VERSIONS OF THIS BOOTSTRAP CODE WRITTEN FOR LATER P?S/8 RELEASES MIGHT SUPPORT
 2358                /       EXTENDED BOOTSTRAP FUNCTIONALITY AS A SUPERSET OF THE STANDARD TC01/TC08
 2359                /       BOOTSTRAP ROUTINE.  THIS ALLOWS BOOTING TO DRIVES OTHER THAN UNIT 0 TO BE USED
 2360                /       AS THE SYSTEM DEVICE.
 2361   
 2362                /       EXTENDED UNIT SUPPORT REQUIRES SUPPLYING A UNIT SELECT VALUE IN THE RANGE OF
 2363                /       1000 THROUGH 7000; THE TC01/TC08 HARDWARE REQUIRES UNIT INFORMATION PASSED IN
 2364                /       AC[0-2] DURING THE "DTLA" OR "DTXA" OPERATION.  THERE MAY BE ADDITIONAL
 2365                /       CONSIDERATIONS AFFECTING OVERALL PROGRAM OPERATION AND CODE EFFICIENCY; THIS
 2366                /       WILL BE DEALT WITH IN FUTURE RELEASES OF THIS DOCUMENT.
 2367   
 2368                /       [NOTE: TRADE-OFFS EXIST WITH REGARD TO DECTAPE STATUS REGISTER "A" ACCESS.
 2369                /       THE "DTLA" OPERATION REQUIRES NO PRIOR KNOWLEDGE OF THE STATUS "A" REGISTER.
 2370                /       THE "DTXA" OPERATION UPDATES THE EXISTING STATUS REGISTER INFORMATION VIA AN
 2371                /       .XOR. TRANSFER BETWEEN THE AC CONTENTS AND THE REGISTER CONTENTS; END-ZONE
 2372                /       HANDLING IS GENERALLY EASIER TO IMPLEMENT USING "DTXA"; THE DIRECTION IS
 2373                /       MERELY INVERTED USING THE CONSTANT 0400 WHEN THE END ERROR IS DETECTED.]
 2374   
 2375                /       UNLIKE THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER EQUIVALENT, THIS ROUTINE IS ONLY USED TO
 2376                /       REBOOT P?S/8 [OR ANY OTHER OPERATING SYSTEM COMPATIBLE WITH THIS BOOTSTRAP
 2377                /       CONVENTION].  AS SUCH, IT DOES NOT CHECK FOR ERRORS; WHEN USED TO REWIND THE
 2378                /       SYSTEM DECTAPE, THE ERROR FLAG WILL RAISE DUE TO CONTROLLER DETECTION OF THE
 2379                /       REVERSE END ZONE.  WHEN USED TO READ BLOCK 0000 MOVING FORWARD OUT OF THE
 2380                /       REVERSE END ZONE, THE WAIT LOOP WILL BE OVERLAID BY THE CODE CONTAINED ON
 2381                /       BLOCK 0000 ACCORDING TO WELL-ESTABLISHED CONVENTIONS.  ALL MEMORY LOCATIONS
 2382                /       OTHER THAN THE WAIT LOOP [WHICH MIGHT LEGITIMATELY BE OVERLAID WITH SLIGHTLY
 2383                /       DIFFERENT CODE] ARE EXPECTED TO BE COMPLETELY DIFFERENT AS A RESULT OF THE
 2384                /       READ OPERATION; ALL SUBSEQUENT ACTIONS ARE DETERMINED BY THE OPERATING SYSTEM
 2385                /       BOOT BLOCK CONTENTS [WHICH ARE LIKELY COMPLETELY DIFFERENT FROM THE REST OF
 2386                /       THE CODE LOADED HERE TO IMPLEMENT THE STAND-ALONE BOOTSTRAP AND SLURP LOADER].
 2387   
 2388                /       THE WAIT ROUTINE AS DEFINED HERE REQUIRES THE NEW CONTENTS OF THE DECTAPE
 2389                /       STATUS REGISTER "A" TO BE PASSED IN THE AC BECAUSE THE "DTLA" INSTRUCTION IS
 2390                /       USED.  AS SUCH, THERE IS NO DEPENDENCY ON PRIOR STATUS REGISTER CONTENTS.
 2391                /       [NOTE: THERE ARE CERTAIN RESTRICTIONS ON CHANGING PARTICULAR STATUS REGISTER
 2392                /       BITS; IF CERTAIN COMBINATIONS OF CHANGES ARE DONE IN AN IMPROPER ORDER, THE
 2393                /       RESULT COULD BE UNCONTROLLED TAPE MOTION.]


