 2488                /       SECTION 3: P?S/8 MODIFIED VERSIONS OF THE DEC STANDARD BIN AND RIM LOADERS.
 2489   
 2490                /       IMAGE OF P?S/8 MODIFIED BIN AND RIM [READ-IN-MODE] LOADERS [07643-07777 ONLY].
 2491   
 2492                /       THIS IS THE P?S/8 MODIFIED VERSION OF THE BIN LOADER FOR STANDALONE USAGE
 2493                /       [SUCH AS RUNNING DIAGNOSTIC PROGRAMS ON BINARY PAPER TAPES] AND THE RIM LOADER
 2494                /       [WHICH IS ESSENTIALLY UNMODIFIED FROM THE DEC ORIGINAL CODE].  THE BIN LOADER
 2495                /       HAS BEEN MADE TO OCCUPY THE SHORTEST OVERALL CODE SPACE BY THE USE OF VARIOUS
 2496                /       OPTIMIZATION TECHNIQUES.
 2497   
 2498                /       THE P?S/8 "BIN" UTILITY WILL LOAD THE STAND-ALONE BOOTSTRAP AND THE BIN AND
 2499                /       RIM LOADERS INTO 07600-07777; AS A RESULT, THE P?S/8 SYSTEM KERNEL IS
 2500                /       DISPLACED FROM MEMORY.  THIS IS ACCOMPLISHED BY SPECIFYING CERTAIN
 2501                /       COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCHES TO P?S/8 BIN.  [NOTE:  BY DEFAULT, P?S/8 BIN
 2502                /       LOADS BINARY FILES INTO MEMORY; BIN CAN ALSO CONVERT BINARY PAPER-TAPES TO
 2503                /       BINARY FILES AND PUNCH BINARY FILES TO PAPER-TAPE IN EITHER BIN OR RIM FORMAT.
 2504                /       FOR A COMPLETE LIST OF OPTIONS FOR THE P?S/8 BIN UTILITY, CONSULT ADVANCED
 2505                /       DOCUMENTATION OF P?S/8 BIN AVAILABLE SEPARATELY.]
 2506   
 2507                /       THE CODING FOR THE P?S/8 VERSION OF THE BIN AND RIM LOADERS IS INCLUDED IN
 2508                /       THIS DOCUMENT TO ILLUSTRATE THE MODIFICATIONS THAT WERE MADE; CERTAIN FEATURES
 2509                /       HAVE BEEN ADDED TO IMPROVE RELIABILITY; OTHERS HAVE BEEN REMOVED FOR DESIGN
 2510                /       REASONS AND/OR TO LIMIT THE AMOUNT OF CODE SPACE USED.
 2511   
 2512                /       THERE ARE CERTAIN TRADEOFFS WITHIN THE DESIGN OF THE BIN AND RIM LOADERS WITH
 2513                /       REGARD TO POTENTIAL INCREASE IN OVERALL PROGRAM SIZE.  THE P?S/8 STAND-ALONE
 2514                /       BOOTSTRAP DESIGN ALSO HAS TRADEOFFS CONCERNING OVERALL PROGRAM SIZE.  SINCE
 2515                /       BOTH PROGRAMS MUST COEXIST WITHIN 07600-07777, ALL RELATED FACTORS MUST BE
 2516                /       CONSIDERED AT ONCE.  CERTAIN OF THESE ISSUES WILL BE DISCUSSED BELOW.
 2517   
 2518                /       NOTABLE FEATURES OF THE P?S/8 VERSION OF THE BIN LOADER.
 2519   
 2520                /       BIN LOADER START AT 07777.
 2521   
 2522                /       THIS FEATURE HAS BEEN RETAINED FOR FULL COMPATIBILITY.  THERE ARE ACTUALLY
 2523                /       SEVERAL DIFFERENT IMPLEMENTATIONS OF WHAT IS COMMONLY REFERRED TO AS THE BIN
 2524                /       LOADER AS DEC [AND OTHERS] HAVE MADE CHANGES TO THIS UTILITY PROGRAM OVER THE
 2525                /       YEARS.  INSTEAD OF DOCUMENTING THE INTERNAL STARTING ADDRESS, LOCATION 07777
 2526                /       CONTAINS A "JMP BEGIN" [5306] INSTRUCTION SPECIFIC TO THIS IMPLEMENTATION.
 2527   
 2528                /       DYNAMIC CHOICE OF LOW-SPEED OR HIGH-SPEED READER.
 2529   
 2530                /       IN MOST OF THE DEC VERSIONS OF THE BIN LOADER, THE CHOICE OF INPUT DEVICE IS
 2531                /       DETERMINED ON THE FRONT PANEL OF THE COMPUTER USING THE HIGH-ORDER BIT OF THE
 2532                /       CONSOLE SWITCH REGISTER.  IN THE P?S/8 IMPLEMENTATION, THIS IS CHOSEN BY
 2533                /       SETTING PROPER COMMAND LINE OPTIONS WHEN INVOKING THE P?S/8 BIN UTILITY
 2534                /       [WHICH IS ALSO USED FOR SEVERAL OTHER MODES OF OPERATION SUCH AS THE LOADING
 2535                /       OF P?S/8 BINARY FILES INTO MEMORY].  ASSUMING APPROPRIATE COMMAND-LINE
 2536                /       PARTICULARS ARE USED TO INVOKE THE LOW-SPEED VERSION OF THE RIM AND BIN
 2537                /       LOADERS, ADDING "/F" TO THE SAME COMMAND CAUSES THE PROGRAM TO USE THE
 2538                /       HIGH-SPEED READER HARDWARE FOR ALL PAPER-TAPE READ FUNCTIONS.  AS NECESSARY,
 2539                /       COMMENTS ARE PROVIDED BELOW TO INDICATE THE ALTERED CONTENTS OF ALL MEMORY
 2540                /       LOCATIONS AFFECTED BY THE USE OF THE HIGH-SPEED READER OPTION.


/    P?S/8 TC01/TC08 SYSTEM HANDLER  P?S PAL V08I    18-AUG-14  PAGE 51

 2542                /       [NOTE: THE P?S/8 VERSION OF THE RIM LOADER IS ESSENTIALLY UNMODIFIED FROM THE
 2543                /       DEC ORIGINAL; HOWEVER, CERTAIN RELEASES OF P?S/8 MAY HAVE NON-STANDARD
 2544                /       HIGH-SPEED READER MODIFICATIONS APPLIED TO RIM WHEN THE "/F" OPTION SWITCH IS
 2545                /       USED ON THE COMMAND LINE INVOKING P?S/8 BIN.  ON THE FEW SYSTEMS TESTED CIRCA
 2546                /       1976, NO PROBLEMS WERE OBSERVED; HOWEVER, THERE MAY BE CERTAIN MODEL-DEPENDENT
 2547                /       PROBLEMS.  NEWER RELEASES WILL CORRECT THESE MINOR ISSUES BY PROVIDING THE
 2548                /       STANDARD HIGH-SPEED READER MODIFICATIONS TO RIM.  WHERE RELEVANT, THE PATCHED
 2549                /       VALUES APPLIED IN THE 1976 RELEASE OF P?S/8 WILL BE DISCUSSED BELOW, ALONG
 2550                /       WITH THE CORRECTED VALUES THAT WILL APPEAR IN A NEWER RELEASE OF P?S/8 BIN.]
 2551   
 2552                /       RUBOUT PROTECTION SUPPORT.
 2553   
 2554                /       AS OF THIS WRITING, THE P?S/8 VERSION OF THE BIN LOADER SUPPORTS THE OBSCURE
 2555                /       FEATURE OF IGNORING IMBEDDED ERROR MESSAGES WITHIN BINARY PAPER TAPES WHEN
 2556                /       PRECEDED AND FOLLOWED BY <RO> [CODE 377] CHARACTERS.  VIRTUALLY ALL RELEASED
 2557                /       VERSIONS OF BIN FORMAT BINARY PAPER TAPES DO NOT REQUIRE THIS FEATURE; IT IS
 2558                /       ONLY POSSIBLE WHEN INCOMPLETELY DEVELOPED PROGRAMS [THAT STILL HAVE DETECTED
 2559                /       ASSEMBLY ERRORS] ARE BEING LOADED [PRESUMABLY FOR DEBUGGING PURPOSES] AND ONLY
 2560                /       IF PUNCHED ON THE CONSOLE TELETYPE PUNCH USING PROGRAMS SUCH AS THE PAPER TAPE
 2561                /       VERSION OF PAL III.  [NOTE: IF THE HIGH-SPEED PUNCH IS USED TO CREATE THE
 2562                /       BINARY PAPER TAPES, ERROR MESSAGES ARE STILL ISSUED TO THE CONSOLE TERMINAL.
 2563                /       AS SUCH, THE PROBLEMATIC CIRCUMSTANCES BEING ADDRESSED COULD NOT OCCUR.]
 2564   
 2565                /       FOR THE VAST MAJORITY OF USERS, THIS FEATURE IS TRULY MEANINGLESS.  AS SUCH,
 2566                /       FUTURE RELEASES OF THE P?S/8 BIN PROGRAM MAY DROP SUPPORT OF THIS FEATURE IN
 2567                /       FAVOR OF SUPPORT OF LONGER REBOOT CODE AND/OR GREATER PROGRAM RELIABILITY.
 2568                /       SHOULD LOADING OF PROBLEMATIC PAPER TAPES BE REQUIRED, THE DEC STANDARD BIN
 2569                /       LOADER CAN BE LOADED BY THE RIM LOADER; IN THE PROCESS, THE P?S/8 RESTART AT
 2570                /       07600 WILL BE DESTROYED; MANUAL ENTRY OF HARDWARE-SPECIFIC BOOTSTRAP CODE FOR
 2571                /       THE P?S/8 SYSTEM DEVICE WILL BE REQUIRED TO RESTART P?S/8.  [NOTE: THE CURRENT
 2572                /       RELEASE OF THE P?S/8 BIN UTILITY CAN CREATE P?S/8 BINARY FILES FROM BINARY
 2573                /       PAPER-TAPE INPUT IN EITHER BIN OR RIM FORMAT USING APPROPRIATE COMMAND-LINE
 2574                /       OPTIONS.  P?S/8 BIN CAN ALSO BE USED WITH ALTERNATE COMMAND-LINE OPTIONS TO
 2575                /       PUNCH BINARY PAPER TAPES FROM THE CONTENTS OF P?S/8 BINARY FILES ON THE
 2576                /       SYSTEM DEVICE.  AS SUCH, P?S/8 CAN BE USED TO NOT ONLY STORE ANY PROBLEMATIC
 2577                /       BINARY DATA, BUT TO ALSO CREATE A DESCENDENT BINARY PAPER-TAPE WITHOUT THE
 2578                /       PROBLEMATIC ERROR MESSAGES; THE RESULTANT PAPER-TAPE WOULD BE SOMEWHAT SHORTER
 2579                /       WITH THE ERROR MESSAGE TEXT REMOVED.]
 2580                /       
 2581                /       BY MINIMIZING THE CODE SPACE OCCUPIED BY THE BIN LOADER TO 07643-07755 [WHICH
 2582                /       IS ADJACENT TO THE RIM LOADER THAT OCCUPIES 07756-07776], A P?S/8 BOOTSTRAP
 2583                /       CAN BE LOADED INTO 07600-07642.  P?S/8 IS NOT LOADED INTO MEMORY WHEN THE BIN
 2584                /       AND RIM LOADERS ARE PRESENT, BUT RESTARTING AT 07600 WILL ALLOW P?S/8 TO BE
 2585                /       REBOOTED WITHOUT MANAL ENTRY OF A TOGGLE-IN BOOTSTRAP.  [NOTE: MOST DEVICES
 2586                /       SPECIFY A SMALL BOOTSTRAP ROUTINE TO RELOAD THE OPERATING SYSTEM, BUT THERE IS
 2587                /       NO CONSISTENCY AS TO THE PROGRAM ADDRESSES OR EXACT OPERATIONAL STEPS USED TO
 2588                /       PERFORM THE BOOTUP OPERATION.  BY PROVIDING A STANDARD RELOAD ROUTINE AT THE
 2589                /       UNIVERSAL EXIT LOCATION OF 07600, P?S/8 CAN MANAGE THE SYSTEM IN THE OVERALL
 2590                /       SENSE.  THIS CONCEPT IS UNIQUE TO P?S/8 AND ITS PREDECESSOR, THE R-L MONITOR
 2591                /       SYSTEM.  HOWEVER, THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM ONLY SUPPORTS SYSTEM RESTART AT 07600
 2592                /       FOR USE WITH THE "SLURP" LOADER FOR BINARY FILES WHILE P?S/8 USES THE SAME
 2593                /       BOOTSTRAP CODE WITH THE BIN AND RIM LOADERS AS WELL.]


