 3489                /       BOOTSTRAP-ONLY WAIT LOOP ROUTINE.
 3490   
 3491                /       THIS IMPLEMENTATION OF A TC01/TC08 WAIT ROUTINE REQUIRES THE NEW CONTENTS OF
 3492                /       THE DECTAPE STATUS REGISTER "A" BE PASSED IN THE AC BECAUSE THE "DTLA" [6766]
 3493                /       INSTRUCTION IS USED; THIS AVOIDS DEPENDENCY ON PRIOR STATUS REGISTER "A"
 3494                /       CONTENTS.  [NOTE: THERE ARE CERTAIN RESTRICTIONS ON UPDATING PARTICULAR
 3495                /       STATUS REGISTER "A" BITS DEPENDING ON THE PRIOR CONTENTS; IF CERTAIN BIT
 3496                /       CHANGES ARE ATTEMPTED IN AN IMPROPER ORDER, THE RESULT COULD BE UNCONTROLLED
 3497                /       TAPE MOTION.]  
 3498   
 3499          7613          SLRPBLK=.                       /ALSO USED FOR LATEST SLURP BLOCK VALUE STORAGE.
 3500   
 3501                /       NOTE: DEPENDING ON THE SPECIFIC CALLER, THE WAIT ROUTINE WILL RETURN DUE TO
 3502                /       END-ZONE ERROR OR WORD-COUNT OVERFLOW WHEN THE DMA OPERATIONS COMPLETE.
 3503   
 3504   07613* 0000  SLWAIT, .-.                             /WAIT ROUTINE.
 3505   07614* 6766          DTLA                            /LOAD STATUS "A" REGISTER WITH PASSED
 3506                                                        /FUNCTION BITS, CLEAR AC.
 3507   07615* 3354          DCA     WC                      /CLEAR WORD COUNT REGISTER NOW IN CASE READING.
 3508   
 3509                /       ENSURE COMPATIBILITY WITH THE STANDARD TC01/TC08 WAIT LOOP.
 3510   
 3511                        IFNZRO  7616-.  <ERROR .>       /MUST BE LOCATED AT 07616.
 3513   
 3514   07616* 6771  SWAITLP,DTSF                            /DECTAPE [OR ERROR] FLAG UP?
 3515   07617* 5216          JMP     SWAITLP                 /FLAG NOT UP YET, KEEP WAITING FOR IT.
 3516   
 3517                /       NOTE: IF ENTERED HERE WHILE A READ OPERATION IS IN PROGRESS, EXECUTION
 3518                /       CONTINUES WITH THE NEW CONTENTS OF MEMORY TAKEN FROM BLOCK 0000 OF THE
 3519                /       JUST-BOOTED SYSTEM DECTAPE; OFTEN A SUBROUTINE HEADER SIMILAR TO "SLWAIT"
 3520                /       [07613] IS PRELOADED WITH A CONTRIVED "RETURN" ADDRESS.  THE P?S/8 SYSTEM
 3521                /       DEVICE HANDLER USES THIS METHOD TO BOOT UP WHEN STARTED BY THIS CODE OR
 3522                /       EQUIVALENT.  [NOTE: EXACT MEMORY LOCATIONS OF THE REST OF THE WAIT ROUTINE IN
 3523                /       THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER MAY VARY; VARIOUS OTHER OPERATING SYSTEMS CAN BE
 3524                /       LOADED BY THIS BOOTSTRAP ROUTINE WITH LITTLE ELSE IN COMMON BESIDES THE WAIT
 3525                /       LOOP REQUIREMENT.]
 3526                /       
 3527                /       THE NEXT INSTRUCTION EXECUTES HARMLESSLY AS "NOP" [7000]; ADDITIONALLY,
 3528                /       IT MUST BE LOCATED AT 07620 TO FORM ANOTHER CONSTANT USED ELSEWHERE.
 3529   
 3530                        IFNZRO  .&177-20        <ERROR  .>
 3532   
 3533   07620* 7000  SL7000, 7000                            /CONSTANT 7000.
 3534   07621* 5613          JMP I   SLWAIT                  /RETURN TO CALLER [IF NOT OVERLAID].
 3535   
 3536   07622* 4002  SL4002, 4002                            /CONSTANT 4002.
 3537   07623* 7577  SL7577, 7577                            /CONSTANT 7577.
 3538   
 3539                /       NOTE: THE BOOTSTRAP CODE IS COMPLETELY CONTAINED ABOVE WITH THE EXCEPTION OF
 3540                /       THE CONSTANT 0220 ("SL220" [7637]) DEFINED ELSEWHERE.  REWORKING THE CODE CAN
 3541                /       SHORTEN THE OVERALL CONTIGUOUS CODE SPACE SIZE IF NECESSARY; HOWEVER, THERE
 3542                /       COULD BE OVERALL CODE SPACE TRADE-OFFS.


/    P?S/8 TC01/TC08 SYSTEM HANDLER  P?S PAL V08I    18-AUG-14  PAGE 70

 3544                /       THE SLURP LOADER COMES HERE TO STOP THE TAPE AFTER THE LATEST FILE HAS BEEN
 3545                /       COMPLETELY LOADED.
 3546   
 3547   07624* 1237  SLPSTP, TAD     SL220/(0220)            /GET READ FUNCTION BITS.
 3548   07625* 6764          DTXA                            /TURN OFF ONLY MOTION AND READ BITS.
 3549   
 3550                /       NOTE: THE CONSTANT 0220 IS USED MERELY IT IS OTHERWISE AVAILABLE; IT IS USED
 3551                /       ELSEWHERE WITHIN THE STAND-ALONE BOOTSTRAP AND SLURP LOADER ROUTINES.
 3552                /       ALTERNATE VALUES CAN BE USED IF AVAILABLE.  USING THE CONSTANT 0220 TURNS OFF
 3553                /       THE TAPE MOTION BIT; THE READ FUNCTION IS CHANGED TO A TAPE MOVE OPERATION.
 3554                /       THE CONSTANT 0200 CAN ALSO BE USED TO MERELY TURN OFF THE MOTION BIT.  EITHER
 3555                /       VALUE CAN BE INCREASED BY 0100 AS SETTING CONTINUOUS MODE IS IGNORED WHEN THE
 3556                /       MOTION BIT IS CLEARED.  (AN ALTERNATE VALUE IS ACTUALLY AVAILABLE, BUT
 3557                /       UNREFERENCED; BY FORCING THE CONSTANT "SL7770" [7770] TO BE PLACED IN 07600,
 3558                /       THE INSTRUCTION LOCATED AT "SLPSTRT+2" [7630] CAN BE USED AS THE CONSTANT 0200
 3559                /       IF DESIRED.)
 3560   
 3561                /       THE CODE FALLS THROUGH TO PROCESS THE NEXT FILE [IF ANY].
 3562   
 3563                /       THE SLURP LOADER STARTS HERE AFTER BEING MOVED TO 07600-07777.
 3564   
 3565   07626* 2353  SLPSTRT,ISZ     SLFLPTR                 /BUMP TO THE NEXT INPUT FILE.
 3566   07627* 1753          TAD I   SLFLPTR                 /GET LATEST FILE HANDLE [SKIPPED IF AT 7777].
 3567   07630* 0200          AND     SL7770/(7770)           /JUST BLOCK BITS.
 3568   07631* 7450          SNA                             /SKIP IF MORE FILES TO LOAD.
 3569   07632* 5346          JMP     SLUSTRT                 /ELSE STARTUP THE USER PROGRAM THERE.
 3570   07633* 3213          DCA     SLRPBLK                 /SAVE FOR SEARCH ROUTINE.
 3571   07634* 1753          TAD I   SLFLPTR                 /GET LATEST FILE HANDLE AGAIN.
 3572   07635* 7012          RTR;RTR                         /MOVE UNIT BITS TO AC[0-2].
        07636* 7012 
 3574   07637* 0220  SL220,  AND     SL7000/(7000)           /ISOLATE UNIT BITS; ALSO CONSTANT 0220.
 3575   
 3576                /       THE ENTIRE STAND-ALONE BOOTSTRAP LOADS ABOVE THIS POINT.  [THE CONSTANT 0220
 3577                /       IS USED WITHIN THE BOOTUP CODE.]
 3578   
 3579          7640          DECTLIM=.                       /UPPER LIMIT FOR CURRENT TC01/TC08 BOOTSTRAP.
 3580   
 3581   07640* 1254          TAD     SL210/(210)             /ADD ON FORWARD MOTION AND SEARCH BITS.
 3582   07641* 6766          DTLA                            /START THE TAPE IN SEARCH MODE, CLEAR AC.
 3583   
 3584                /       SINCE THE AC IS CLEAR, FORWARD TAPE MOTION WILL BE USED AS THE CURRENT TAPE
 3585                /       DRIVE IS SEARCHED FOR THE INITIAL FILE BLOCK.  IN THE GENERAL CASE, THIS WOULD
 3586                /       NOT BE RECOMMENDED; HOWEVER, ALL TFS BINARY FILES OR EQUIVALENT STORAGE IN
 3587                /       EXTENDED DIRECTORIES [OTHER THAN % AND $] ARE LOCATED FORWARD OF THE CURRENT
 3588                /       TAPE POSITION WHERE THE P?S/8 BIN UTILITY [WHICH LOADS THIS PROGRAM INTO
 3589                /       MEMORY] IS LOCATED.  APPENDIX "N" DISCUSSES A TECHNIQUE TO OPTIMIZE SYSTEM
 3590                /       PERFORMANCE WHEN USING THE SLURP LOADER AS DEFINED IN THIS VERSION.  [NOTE:
 3591                /       FUTURE RELEASES MAY DIFFER ON THIS POINT RENDERING THE METHODS DESCRIBED
 3592                /       EITHER OBSOLETE OR SUPERFLUOUS.]


/    P?S/8 TC01/TC08 SYSTEM HANDLER  P?S PAL V08I    18-AUG-14  PAGE 71

 3594                /       ADDITIONAL SPECIFIC SEARCH ROUTINE CONSIDERATIONS.
 3595   
 3596                /       1) DUE TO SEVERELY LIMITED CODE SPACE, THE CAPABILITIES OF THIS SEARCH ROUTINE
 3597                /          ARE INFERIOR TO THE CODING USED IN THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER:
 3598   
 3599                /          A) THERE IS NO RECOVERY FROM ERRORS SINCE THERE SHOULD NEVER BE AN END-ZONE
 3600                /             ERROR.  WITHOUT THE ABILITY TO TURN THE TAPE AROUND AND OTHERWISE IGNORE
 3601                /             THIS SITUATION, IT IS NOT POSSIBLE TO RECOVER FROM THIS CONDITION
 3602                /             WITHOUT RESTARTING THE SYSTEM MANUALLY THUS ABORTING THE SLURP LOADER.
 3603                /             HOWEVER, THIS ONLY AFFECTS DECTAPE BLOCKS HIGHER THAN ANY VALID FILE
 3604                /             BLOCK OR BLOCKS LESS THAN 0002.  NONE OF THESE ARE VALID FILE BLOCKS FOR
 3605                /             TFS FILES OR EQUIVALENT; THIS CONSIDERATION IS THUS IRRELEVANT TO THE
 3606                /             SLURP LOADER.
 3607   
 3608                /          B) SINCE VERY LOW BLOCK NUMBERS ARE NEVER SEARCHED FOR, IT IS ACCEPTABLE TO
 3609                /             SEARCH FOR DECTAPE BLOCKS USING SIGNED ARITHMETIC; THIS LIMITS THE
 3610                /             LARGEST VALID SEARCHABLE BLOCK TO 3776.  THE LONGEST KNOWN PHYSICAL
 3611                /             DECTAPES ARE LESS THAN 3400 BLOCKS; NO PROBLEMS ARE EXPECTED UNLESS THE
 3612                /             SLURP LOADER IS USED ON A COMPUTER SIMULATOR THAT ALLOWS FOR LARGER
 3613                /             DECTAPES.  [IF NEED BE, P?S/8 BIN CAN BE INVOKED WITH THE "/V" SWITCH
 3614                /             SET TO FORCE THE USAGE OF THE VIRTUAL BINARY FILE LOADER; THIS WILL
 3615                /             ALLOW LOADING OF BINARY FILES LOCATED UP TO BLOCK 7776, THE INHERENT
 3616                /             LIMITATION OF THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER SEARCH ROUTINE.]
 3617   
 3618                /          C) THE USUAL UNDERSHOOT FACTOR IS USED TO ALLOW THE TAPE TO TURN AROUND
 3619                /             WHEN LOCATED FORWARD OF THE DESIRED DECTAPE BLOCK; HOWEVER, ALL FILE
 3620                /             SEARCHES ARE INITIATED IN THE FORWARD DIRECTION.  SUBSEQUENT SEARCH
 3621                /             OPERATIONS WILL CORRECTLY TURN THE TAPE AROUND TO LOCATE THE DESIRED
 3622                /             DECTAPE BLOCK WHILE MOVING FORWARD; HOWEVER, THE SEARCH MAY PHYSICALLY
 3623                /             START FORWARD THEN IMMEDIATELY TURN AROUND DUE TO THE LIMITATIONS OF
 3624                /             ALWAYS STARTING THE SEARCH INITIALLY FORWARD.  THIS SLIGHT POTENTIAL
 3625                /             OVERHEAD IS STILL OUTWEIGHED BY THE MUCH LARGER OVERHEAD ASSOCIATED WITH
 3626                /             ALL OTHER FORMS OF BINARY LOADING [SUCH AS USING THE VIRTUAL LOADER].
 3627   
 3628                /             WHEN CONTIGUOUS FILES ARE LOADED IN THE USUAL MANNER, THE OVERHEAD DUE
 3629                /             TO INITIAL FORWARD SEARCH DIRECTION FOR THE SECONDARY FILES CANNOT BE
 3630                /             DISCERNED BY THE USER UNLESS AN ACCURATE STOPWATCH IS USED; MOST OF THE
 3631                /             OVERHEAD IS UNAVOIDABLE AND ACTUALLY CAUSED BY TAPE COASTING.  THE
 3632                /             EXAMPLES DISCUSSED IN APPENDIX "N" OVERCOME BOTH THE ISSUE OF TAPE
 3633                /             COASTING AND DELIBERATE FORWARD INITIAL SEARCH DIRECTION [WHICH IS
 3634                /             CONVERTED FROM A SMALL LIABILITY INTO AN ASSET].  TAKING ADVANTAGE OF
 3635                /             THE FIXED SIZE OF TFS FILES, PALPABLE PERFORMANCE IMPROVEMENT IS
 3636                /             IMMEDIATELY NOTICED.


/    P?S/8 TC01/TC08 SYSTEM HANDLER  P?S PAL V08I    18-AUG-14  PAGE 72

 3638                /       2) ALL DETECTED ERRORS ARE FATAL.  IF THERE ARE HARDWARE CONSIDERATIONS THAT
 3639                /          PREVENT THE USE OF THE SLURP LOADER, THE USER IS DIRECTED TO USE THE
 3640                /          VIRTUAL LOADER AS DESCRIBED IN 1B) ABOVE.  USING THE VIRTUAL BINARY FILE
 3641                /          LOADER REQUIRES WRITE-ENABLE ON THE DECTAPE DRIVE; OVERALL PERFORMANCE WILL
 3642                /          BE DEGRADED COMPARED TO THE SLURP LOADER; HOWEVER, ALL TAPE ERRORS CAN BE
 3643                /          RETRIED UNTIL SUCCESSFUL.
 3644   
 3645                /          NOTE: USING A SYSTEM EXHIBITING HARDWARE PROBLEMS SHOULD BE CONSIDERED A
 3646                /          TEMPORARY MEASURE AS THE OCCURRENCE OF EXCESSIVE ERRORS IS A CLEAR SIGN OF
 3647                /          IMPENDING HARDWARE FAILURE OF THE TAPE GUIDES OR DECTAPE MEDIA.  IN SOME
 3648                /          CASES, THE ONLY REMEDY IS PROPER DRIVE MAINTENANCE, WHICH COULD INCLUDE
 3649                /          THOROUGH TAPE AND TAPE GUIDE CLEANING AND PERHAPS HEAD SKEW ALIGNMENT OR
 3650                /          REPLACEMENT OF TAPE GUIDE PARTS OR THE TAPE MEDIA ITSELF DEPENDING ON THE
 3651                /          SEVERITY OF THE PROBLEM.
 3652   
 3653                /          USE OF THE VIRTUAL LOADER SHOULD NOT BE CONSIDERED AS A SUBSTITUTE FOR
 3654                /          PROPER PHYSICAL MAINTENANCE!  OCCURRENCE OF FREQUENT ERRORS IS A SIGN OF A
 3655                /          SERIOUS HARDWARE PROBLEM THAT WILL ONLY TEND TO GET WORSE WITH TIME AND
 3656                /          USAGE AS THE UNDERLYING CONDITIONS WORSEN.
