/    P?S/8 TC01/TC08 SYSTEM HANDLER  P?S PAL V08I    18-AUG-14  PAGE 84

 4211                /       SECTION 6: P?S/8 KEYBOARD MONITOR REWIND AND UNLOAD ROUTINES FOR TC01/TC08.
 4212   
 4213                /       THESE ARE THE ACTUAL REWIND AND UNLOAD ROUTINES TAKEN FROM A 1976 P?S/8 SYSTEM
 4214                /       DECTAPE IMAGE [KNOWN TO NOT BE A FINAL RELEASE].
 4215   
 4216                /       THIS SMALL ROUTINE IS THE P?S/8 KEYBOARD MONITOR AND IMBEDDED EDITOR CODING
 4217                /       TO HANDLE CONTROL-R AND CONTROL-T CHARACTERS WHICH CAN BE TYPED DURING THE
 4218                /       ENTRY OF ALL FORMS OF TEXT ENTRY INCLUDING EXECUTION-CLASS COMMANDS NOT YET
 4219                /       COMPLETED BY PRESSING THE RETURN KEY.
 4220   
 4221                /       CONTROL-R IS MEANT TO BE USED TO REWIND THE CURRENT SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER
 4222                /       DRIVE UNIT [ASSUMING THE HARDWARE IS SOME FORM OF TAPE DEVICE].  SIMILARLY,
 4223                /       CONTROL-T IS MEANT TO BE USED TO UNLOAD THE SAME DEVICE.  NOT ALL SYSTEMS
 4224                /       SUPPORT THESE COMMANDS EQUALLY; ON SOME SYSTEMS THE COMMANDS ARE VIRTUALLY
 4225                /       INTERCHANGEABLE; ON OTHER SYSTEMS BOTH COMMANDS ARE IGNORED.
 4226   
 4227                /       EACH SPECIFIC HARDWARE-DEPENDENT RELEASE OF P?S/8 SUPPORTS A CUSTOM VERSION OF
 4228                /       THIS CODE TAILORED FOR THE SYSTEM DEVICE HARDWARE OF THAT PARTICULAR SYSTEM
 4229                /       [IF THE HARDWARE SUPPORTS THESE COMMANDS AT ALL].  THE ACTIONS TAKEN ARE
 4230                /       PARTICULAR TO THE HARDWARE CONFIGURATION.
 4231   
 4232                /       THE CODE DECRIBED HERE IS FOR THE TC01/TC08 DECTAPE CONFIGURATION.  ANY MIX OF
 4233                /       TU55 AND TU56 DRIVES IS SUPPORTED; HOWEVER, THE EXACT ACTIONS TAKEN ARE
 4234                /       DEPENDENT ON THE DRIVE TYPE:
 4235   
 4236                /       WHEN CONTROL-R IS TYPED, THE CURRENT TAPE DRIVE UNIT IS REWOUND TOWARDS THE
 4237                /       REVERSE END ZONE.  CONTROL IS IMMEDIATELY RETURNED TO THE KEYBOARD MONITOR TO
 4238                /       ALLOW ADDITIONAL KEYBOARD INPUT WHILE THE TAPE IS REWINDING.  WHEN THE TAPE
 4239                /       ENTERS THE END ZONE, THE CONTROLLER DETECTS THIS AS AN END ERROR, AND STOPS
 4240                /       THE TAPE AUTOMATICALLY.
 4241   
 4242                /       THIS ALLOWS THE USER TO TYPE ADDITIONAL COMMANDS DURING THE TAPE REWIND
 4243                /       OPERATION TAKING ADVANTAGE OF OVERLAPPED OPERATION.  THIS COULD INCLUDE
 4244                /       ENTERING AN EXECUTION-CLASS COMMAND KNOWN TO REQUIRE ACCESS TO BLOCKS NEAR THE
 4245                /       PHYSICAL BEGINNING OF THE TAPE; BY INITIATING A REWIND DURING THE COMMAND
 4246                /       ENTRY, SIGNIFICANT WINDING TIME CAN BE ACHIEVED BEFORE THE COMMAND IS
 4247                /       COMPLETELY ENTERED.
 4248   
 4249                /       SHOULD THE COMMAND REQUIRE READING IN PART OF THE SYSTEM DEVICE, THE REWIND
 4250                /       OPERATION IS CANCELLED BY THE CALL TO THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER.  [NOTE: THIS
 4251                /       IS TRUE FOR THE TC01/TC08 VERSION OF THE REWIND ROUTINE AS DESCRIBED HERE;
 4252                /       OTHER IMPLEMENTATIONS MAY NOT DUPLICATE THE COMMAND ACTION SUFFICIENTLY.  FOR
 4253                /       EXAMPLE, THE TD8E VERSION OF THE REWIND ROUTINE MUST MONITOR THE TAPE POSITION
 4254                /       UNTIL THE END ZONE IS LOCATED; AS SUCH, OVERLAP IS NOT POSSIBLE ON THAT
 4255                /       CONFIGURATION.]


/    P?S/8 TC01/TC08 SYSTEM HANDLER  P?S PAL V08I    18-AUG-14  PAGE 85

 4257                /       WHEN CONTROL-T IS TYPED, THE CURRENT TAPE DRIVE IS REWOUND; HOWEVER, THE
 4258                /       ROUTINE WAITS FOR THE END ERROR; AS SUCH, OVERLAPPED OPERATIONS ARE NOT
 4259                /       POSSIBLE.
 4260   
 4261                /       ADDITIONAL OPERATIONS ARE PERFORMED AFTER THE END ZONE IS DETECTED FOR THE
 4262                /       PURPOSE OF FORCING THE TAPE OFF THE TAKE-UP REEL [CAUSING A FULL TAPE UNLOAD].
 4263                /       WHAT HAPPENS NEXT DEPENDS ON THE DRIVE TYPE:
 4264   
 4265                /       1) IF THE SELECTED DRIVE IS A TU55, ADDITIONAL COMMANDS ARE ISSUED TO MODIFY
 4266                /          TAPE DIRECTION AND MOTION BITS FORCING THE TAPE REELS TO LOCK.
 4267   
 4268                /       2) IF THE SELECTED DRIVE IS A TU56 [WHICH LACKS MECHANICAL BRAKING], THE TAPE
 4269                /          REELS ROTATE UNCONTROLLABLY UNTIL THE USER RESETS THE DRIVE; THE ADDITIONAL
 4270                /          COMMANDS ARE IGNORED.
 4271   
 4272                /       AFTER THE UNLOAD OPERATION HAS COMPLETED, CONTROL IS RETURNED TO THE KEYBOARD
 4273                /       MONITOR TO ALLOW ADDITIONAL KEYBOARD INPUT.
 4274   
 4275                /       IMPLEMENTATION OF SPECIFIC REWIND/UNLOAD ROUTINES IN THE KEYBOARD MONITOR.
 4276   
 4277                /       HISTORICALLY, P?S/8 SYSTEM GENERATION CONSISTED OF PLACING ALL COMPONENTS
 4278                /       AFFECTED BY CHOICE OF SYSTEM DEVICE INTO MEMORY AT THE SAME TIME.  THE
 4279                /       SPECIFIC CODE PARTICULAR TO THE CHOSEN DEVICE IS THEN OVERLAID OVER THE BASIC
 4280                /       ROUTINES TO PRODUCE A CUSTOMIZED SYSTEM.
 4281   
 4282                /       TO CUSTOMIZE P?S/8 IN THE FUTURE, NEW MECHANISMS NEED TO BE DEFINED TO
 4283                /       COMPLETELY DEFINE THE SYSTEM SPECIFICS.  SYSTEMS SUCH AS OS/8 MERELY NEED TO
 4284                /       DEFINE A SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER; OTHER SYSTEM COMPONENTS SUCH AS THE REWIND AND
 4285                /       UNLOAD ROUTINES DO NOT EXIST ELSEWHERE.
 4286   
 4287                /       FOR THE PRESENT, ACCESS TO THE SOURCE CODE IS NEEDED, INCLUDING ALL CODE
 4288                /       SPECIFIC TO THE HARDWARE.  IN SOME CASES, THIS WAS PARTIALLY CREATED BY HAND
 4289                /       OR TRANSFERRED BY IMAGE COPYING FROM OTHER SYSTEMS THAT SUPPORTED P?S/8 BUT
 4290                /       NOT THE CODE SPECIFICS [SUCH AS CREATING TD8E SYSTEMS ON THE TC01/TC08-BASED
 4291                /       SYSTEM].
 4292   
 4293                /       FUTURE SYSTEM GENERATION TECHNIQUES MAY SEPARATE THE SPECIFICS OF THE HARDWARE
 4294                /       CONFIGURATION TARGET FROM THE CURRENT SYSTEM CONFIGURATION.  THIS WILL ALLOW
 4295                /       IMAGING OF A SYSTEM TO EVENTUALLY BE TRANSFERRED TO THE TARGET HARDWARE
 4296                /       CONFIGURATION.  APPENDIX "H" DISCUSSES CERTAIN SYSTEM GENERATION TECHNIQUES
 4297                /       THAT APPLY TO THE REWIND AND UNLOAD ROUTINES AS WELL AS ALL OTHER
 4298                /       HARDWARE-SPECIFIC CONSIDERATIONS.
 4299   
 4300                /       NOTE: OS/8 SUPPORTS A COMMAND TO REWIND A TC01/TC08 DECTAPE WHICH CAN BE USED
 4301                /       FOR ANALOGOUS PURPOSES, AND A SEPARATE UNLOAD COMMAND FOR THE TC01/TC08 THAT
 4302                /       WILL ALSO WAIT UNTIL THE TAPE UNLOAD OPERATION COMPLETES.  BOTH OF THESE
 4303                /       SYSTEMS SHOULD NOT EXECUTE THE TC01/TC08-SPECIFIC ROUTINES ON CERTAIN
 4304                /       CONFIGURATIONS OF THE PDP-12; THE COMPUTER WILL HANG IF THE "DTLA" [6766]
 4305                /       OPERATION IS ATTEMPTED.


