 6181                /          [NOTE: SINCE THE MDC8 CAN SUPPORT PRIORITY 0 OR 1, IT IS POSSIBLE TO HAVE
 6182                /          TWO MDC8 SUBSYSTEMS ON THE SAME MACHINE; THIS IS THE RECOMMENDED WAY TO
 6183                /          SUPPORT OMNI-8 TO AVOID USING DEC PERIPHERAL HARDWARE [ACCORDING TO CESI].
 6184                /          BY USING P?S/8 TO SUPPORT OMNI-8 DEVELOPMENT, THIS BECOMES SUPERFLUOUS AS
 6185                /          ALL FUNCTIONS CAN BE SUPPORTED ON ONE MDC8.]
 6186   
 6187                /          CHARLES LASNER HAS WRITTEN OS/8 AND P?S/8 SYSTEM AND NON-SYSTEM HANDLERS
 6188                /          FOR BOTH OS/8 AND P?S/8 WHEN USED WITH THE 128 WORD BLOCKSIZE MDC8 VARIANT.
 6189                /          DUE TO THE EXCELLENT DESIGN OF THE MDC8, OS/8 CAN BE RUN IN 8K AND P?S/8
 6190                /          CAN BE RUN IN 4K ON THIS VARIANT OF THE HARDWARE.  [NOTE: MEMORY
 6191                /          CONTROLLERS MUST BE KM8A-COMPLIANT UP TO 32K FOR THESE SYSTEMS TO OPERATE.]
 6192   
 6193                /          [NOTE: CHARLES LASNER DEVELOPED THE MDC8 UNIVERSAL BOOTUP CONVENTIONS FOR
 6194                /          ALL SOFTWARE CONFIGURATIONS INCLUDING OMNI-8; THE ACTUAL CODE IS ONLY
 6195                /          SLIGHTLY LONGER THAN THE RK8E BOOTUP CONVENTIONS.  MULTIPLE OPERATING
 6196                /          SYSTEMS ARE SUPPORTABLE USING MENU-8, A MASTER BOOT MENU SYSTEM VAGUELY
 6197                /          ANALOGOUS TO MASTER MENU FOR THE DECMATE II AND DECMATE III+ WITH THE RD51
 6198                /          HARD DISK CONTROLLER OPTION.  ALL DEVICE HANDLERS USE A DOUBLE-PRECISION
 6199                /          OFFSET WORD STORED WITHIN THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER RESIDENT IN 07600-07777
 6200                /          TO DETERMINE EXACTLY WHERE THE CORRESPONDING DISK STORAGE IS.  A TYPICAL
 6201                /          CONFIGURATION HAS MENU-8 AS THE ABSOLUTE BOOTUP SYSTEM WHICH IN TURN CAN
 6202                /          BOOT OTHER SYSTEMS BY SETTING THE APPROPRIATE OFFSET IN A LONGER BOOTUP
 6203                /          ROUTINE.  IF MENU-8 IS NOT USED, ANY ONE OPERATING SYSTEM CAN BE RESIDENT
 6204                /          IN THE ABSOLUTE BOOTUP AREA; BY USING THE LONGER BOOTUP ROUTINE, MULTIPLE
 6205                /          OPERATING SYSTEMS CAN EXIST ON THE MDC8 DISK.  THE PRIMARY OPERATING SYSTEM
 6206                /          OUGHT TO BE ABLE TO RUN THE LONGER BOOTUP PROGRAM TO ALLOW MULTIPLE
 6207                /          SYSTEMS TO COEXIST ON THIS SYSTEM; BY USING MENU-8, THE SHORTEST BOOTSTRAP
 6208                /          CAN BE USED TO ACCESS ALL OPERATING SYSTEMS.  THE SHORTEST BOOTSTRAP CAN
 6209                /          BE LOADED INTO ANY OF THE HARDWARE LOADERS FOR THE OMNIBUS INCLUDING THE
 6210                /          MI8E BOARD FOR THE PDP-8/E; THE MDC8 WOULD HAVE TO BE ADDED TO AN -8/A BOX
 6211                /          IN A MANNER SIMILAR TO THE FPP-8/E.]
 6212   
 6213                /       WITHIN P?S/8, THE PHYSICAL SIZE OF MEMORY CAN BE AS LARGE AS 32K; ON SYSTEMS
 6214                /       THAT RUN IN 4K, FIELD 0 COULD BE THE LARGEST MEMORY FIELD AVAILABLE; THE
 6215                /       LARGEST FIELD POSSIBLE IS FIELD 7.  AS P?S/8 BOOTS UP, THIS VALUE IS
 6216                /       DYNAMICALLY CALCULATED USING CODING KNOWN TO WORK PROPERLY ON ALL MODELS; THE
 6217                /       VALUE IS STORED INTO BITS[0-2] OF THE CORE SIZE AND STATUS WORD.


/    P?S/8 TC01/TC08 SYSTEM HANDLER  P?S PAL V08I    18-AUG-14  PAGE 124

 6219                /       THE LOGICAL HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD IS DETERMINED AFTER THE PHYSICAL HIGHEST
 6220                /       MEMORY FIELD IS CALCULATED.  CERTAIN P?S/8 COMPONENTS OCCUPY PART OF THE
 6221                /       PHYSICAL HIGHEST FIELD; IF ANY OF THESE COMPONENTS IS PRESENT, THE LOGICAL
 6222                /       HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD IS SET TO ONE MEMORY FIELD LOWER.  ANY OF THE FOLLOWING
 6223                /       COMPONENTS BEING PRESENT IN MEMORY WILL FORCE THE LOWERING OF THE MAXIMUM
 6224                /       AVAILABLE MEMORY BY ONE MEMORY FIELD:
 6225   
 6226                /       1) THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER REQUIRES AN EXTENSION; THIS RESERVES LOCATIONS
 6227                /          6000-7777 IN THE HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD.
 6228   
 6229                /       2) THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IS ENABLED; THIS OCCUPIES 0000-5377 OR
 6230                /          0000-5777 IN THE HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD.
 6231   
 6232                /       3) THE P?S/8 SHELL OVERLAY IS ENABLED AND THE FILE AND COMMUNICATIONS AREA IS
 6233                /          LOADED INTO 5400-5777 OF THE HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD.  [NOTE: THE SHELL DESIGN
 6234                /          IS NEWER THAN CERTAIN RELEASES OF THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY.  ALL CURRENT
 6235                /          DEVICE SUPPORT WITHIN THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY CAN BE ACHIEVED WITHOUT
 6236                /          USING 5400-5777; HOWEVER, THE OVERLAY MUST BE SLIGHTLY MODIFIED TO CONFORM
 6237                /          TO THE NEW REQUIREMENT.  THE LARGEST KNOWN IMPLEMENTATION IS THE VT8E
 6238                /          CONFIGURATION WITH INTERNAL DEVICE 66 SUPPORT.  ALL AVAILABLE MEMORY
 6239                /          THROUGH 5777 WAS USED AS ORIGINALLY RELEASED; HOWEVER, THE HIGHEST
 6240                /          ADDRESSES ARE ONLY USED TO ALLOW THE INTERNAL PRINT BUFFER TO BE NEEDLESSLY
 6241                /          LARGE.  THE REST OF AVAILABLE MEMORY WAS USED TO DEFINE THE PRINT BUFFER;
 6242                /          HOWEVER, THE FULL EFFECT OF PRINT BUFFERING CAN BE ACHIEVED WITH FAR LESS
 6243                /          BUFFER SPACE.  AS LONG AS JUST OVER TWO COMPLETE PRINTABLE LINES CAN BE
 6244                /          STORED, PRINT BUFFERING WILL BE 100% EFFECTIVE; LARGER BUFFERS COULD
 6245                /          ACTUALLY BE SLIGHTLY LESS EFFICIENT.  THUS, LIMITING THE PRINT BUFFER TO
 6246                /          APPROXIMATELY 270 CHARACTERS WILL FULLY SUPPORT WIDE-CARRIAGE PRINTERS; THE
 6247                /          REST OF AVAILABLE MEMORY CAN BE RESERVED FOR THE POTENTIAL NEEDS OF THE
 6248                /          SHELL-RELATED RESOURCE.  THIS PROBLEM WILL BE REMEDIED IN THE NEXT FULL
 6249                /          RELEASE OF P?S/8.]
 6250   
 6251                /       NOTE: ALL THREE OF THE POTENTIAL SYSTEM COMPONENTS OUTLINED ABOVE ARE
 6252                /       DESCRIBED BELOW IN GREATER DETAIL.
 6253   
 6254                /       WITH THE EXCEPTION OF THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER EXTENSION, ALL OF THE ABOVE
 6255                /       SYSTEM COMPONENTS MAY BE DISABLED; SHOULD THE ENTIRE MEMORY FIELD BECOME
 6256                /       AVAILABLE, THE LOGICAL HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD CAN BE RECALCULATED TO MATCH THE
 6257                /       HIGHEST PHYSICAL MEMORY FIELD.  [NOTE: THE P?S/8 "CORE" UTILITY CAN BE USED TO
 6258                /       MAKE ALL ADJUSTMENTS TO MEMORY FIELD PARAMETERS; THE COMMAND "CORE ALL" WILL
 6259                /       ALWAYS SET THE MAXIMUM AVAILABLE MEMORY.  SEE BELOW FOR MORE DETAILS OF THE
 6260                /       P?S/8 CORE COMMAND.]
 6261   
 6262                /       THE LOGICAL HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD IS USED BY ALL SYSTEM COMPONENTS AND
 6263                /       CONFORMING PROGRAMS TO DETERMINE POTENTIAL ADDITIONAL MEMORY ALLOCATIONS
 6264                /       BEYOND THE STANDARD AVAILABILITY OF THE FIRST 4K OF MEMORY REQUIRED TO RUN
 6265                /       P?S/8.  THE LOGICAL HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD CAN BE SET BY THE P?S/8 CORE UTILITY
 6266                /       TO ANY VALUE BETWEEN FIELD 0 AND THE FIELD INDICATED IN THE LOGICAL HIGHEST
 6267                /       MEMORY FIELD.  ONLY COMPLETELY AVAILABLE FIELDS ARE CONSIDERED.  BY
 6268                /       ARTIFICIALLY LOWERING THE QUANTITY OF EXTENDED MEMORY AVAILABLE, THE EXISTING
 6269                /       CONTENTS OF HIGHER MEMORY FIELDS CAN BE PROTECTED; PERFORMANCE OF PROGRAMS
 6270                /       THAT DYNAMICALLY ALLOCATE MEMORY BUFFERS CAN BE TESTED AS IF RUNNING ON ACTUAL
 6271                /       SMALLER SYSTEMS.


/    P?S/8 TC01/TC08 SYSTEM HANDLER  P?S PAL V08I    18-AUG-14  PAGE 125

 6273                /       BASIC P?S/8 PROGRAMS ARE ALLOWED TO INSPECT THE HIGHEST PHYSICAL MEMORY FIELD
 6274                /       DATA TO DETERMINE IF A PARTIAL FIELD IS AVAILABLE.  [NOTE: NOT EVERY PROGRAM
 6275                /       IS CAPABLE OF USING A PARTIAL MEMORY FIELD; P?S/8 PAL IS A NOTABLE EXAMPLE OF
 6276                /       A PROGRAM THAT CAN USE A PARTIAL MEMORY FIELD TO INCREASE THE MAXIMUM SIZE OF
 6277                /       THE SYMBOL TABLE.]  IF THE LOGICAL HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD IS ONE MEMORY FIELD
 6278                /       LOWER THAN THE HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD, 3K OF MEMORY MIGHT BE AVAILABLE IF THE
 6279                /       LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IS NOT PRESENT.  [THIS CAN BE DETERMINED AS DESCRIBED
 6280                /       BELOW.]  THIS WOULD ONLY APPLY IF THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER REQUIRES AN
 6281                /       EXTENDED MEMORY SEGMENT OF 6000-7777 IN THE HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD.
 6282   
 6283                /       NOTE: P?S/8 SYSTEMS RELEASED PRIOR TO THE ADDITION OF THE P?S/8 SHELL OVERLAY
 6284                /       ARE NOT AWARE OF THE SHELL FILE AND COMMUNICATIONS AREA POTENTIAL RESERVATION
 6285                /       OF LOCATIONS 5400-5777 IN THE HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD; HOWEVER, THIS IS MOOT
 6286                /       WITHIN THE BASIC P?S/8 SYSTEM.  LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY DESIGN COMPATIBLE WITH
 6287                /       THE POTENTIAL OF THE SHELL OVERLAY WILL AVOID CONFLICT IN THIS TWO-PAGE AREA.
 6288                /       AS SUCH, PROGRAMS RUN UNDER THE SHELL OVERLAY MUST CHECK FURTHER TO DETERMINE
 6289                /       IF THE FILE AND COMMUNICATIONS AREA IS RESIDENT IN THESE LOCATIONS WHICH IS A
 6290                /       CONFIGURATION PARAMETER OF THE SHELL ITSELF.  [NOTE: THE STATUS OF THE FILE
 6291                /       AND COMMUNICATIONS AREA CAN BE DETERMINED BY INSPECTION OF BIT[0] OF THE
 6292                /       "SOUTCT" [07607] STATUS WORD; HOWEVER, THIS IS ONLY MEANINGFUL FROM THE SHELL
 6293                /       ENVIRONMENT.  SHELL-BASED PROGRAMS ATTEMPTING TO ALLOCATE ADDITIONAL MEMORY
 6294                /       IN A PARTIAL HIGHEST PHYSICAL FIELD MUST BE PREPARED TO LIMIT ALLOCATION TO
 6295                /       0000-5377 OR 0000-5777 AS REQUIRED.]
 6296   
 6297                /       P?S/8 CORE UTILITY.
 6298   
 6299                /       BY INVOKING THE CORE UTILITY WITH APPROPRIATE ARGUMENTS, THE CURRENT LOGICAL
 6300                /       CORE SIZE CAN BE SET TO ANY VALUE BETWEEN 0 AND THE MAXIMUM LOGICAL CORE SIZE
 6301                /       ALLOWED ON THE CURRENT SYSTEM.
 6302   
 6303                /       DELIBERATELY LOWERING THE LOGICAL CORE SIZE CAN BE USEFUL FOR DEBUGGING,
 6304                /       TESTING OR PROTECTING DATA RESIDENT IN HIGH MEMORY [SUCH AS AN IMAGE OF THE
 6305                /       MR8E-C ROM LOADED INTO WRITABLE MEMORY ON TD8E-BASED SYSTEMS UNDER TEST].
 6306   
 6307                /       "CORE" [WITHOUT ARGUMENTS] WILL DISPLAY THE CURRENT SETTING OF THE THREE
 6308                /       MEMORY SIZE PARAMETERS.  AN OPTIONAL ARGUMENT CAN BE USED [SUCH AS "CORE 5"]
 6309                /       TO LIMIT MEMORY TO ANY ALLOWED VALUE.  [NOTE: ERROR MESSAGES WILL BE ISSUED
 6310                /       WHEN ATTEMPTING TO USE INVALID ARGUMENTS FOR THE CURRENT SYSTEM OR ANY ATTEMPT
 6311                /       TO USE INVALID SYNTAX; THE ONLY VALID ARGUMENTS ARE "0" THROUGH "7" AND "ALL";
 6312                /       NUMERIC VALUES MUST BE VALID FOR THE CURRENT SYSTEM CONFIGURATION.]  [NOTE:
 6313                /       OS/8 SUPPORTS A VAGUE ANALOGY TO THE CORE COMMAND; HOWEVER, THE LOGICAL SIZE
 6314                /       OF OS/8 MUST BE SET TO A MINIMUM OF 1 BECAUSE OS/8 REQUIRES AT LEAST 8K OF
 6315                /       MEMORY TO OPERATE; IF THE OS/8 LOGICAL CORE SIZE IS NOT SET, EVERY PROGRAM
 6316                /       SEEKING ADDITIONAL MEMORY MUST PROVIDE ITS OWN CORE SIZING ROUTINE OR ASSUME
 6317                /       ONLY 8K IS AVAILABLE; NO OS/8 CONFIGURATION EXISTS WITH ONLY 4K AVAILABLE.
 6318                /       ALL CORE SIZE MANAGEMENT IN OS/8 MUST BE ACHIEVED IN THREE BITS USED FOR ALL
 6319                /       PURPOSES; THE ADDITIONAL MEMORY SIZE CONCEPTS SUPPORTED BY P?S/8 ARE
 6320                /       CONCEPTUALLY IMPOSSIBLE WITHIN OS/8.]


