 8356                / 11) LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY
 8357   
 8358                /     THE P?S/8 LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IS AN OPTIONAL COMPONENT OF P?S/8 THAT
 8359                /     PROVIDES ALTERNATE CONSOLE AND LINEPRINTER SERVICES TO ALL COMPLIANT
 8360                /     PROGRAMS THROUGHOUT P?S/8 [INCLUDING USER-WRITTEN PROGRAMS].  EXTENDED
 8361                /     MEMORY IS REQUIRED TO ENABLE THE OVERLAY; AS A RESULT, THE LOGICAL MEMORY
 8362                /     SIZE MUST BE REDUCED BY ONE ENTIRE MEMORY FIELD [UNLESS ALREADY REDUCED BY
 8363                /     ANOTHER SYSTEM COMPONENT SUCH AS AN EXTENDED SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER].
 8364   
 8365                /     COMPLIANT PROGRAMS REPLACE THEIR INTERNAL CODE FOR THE DEVICE 03/04
 8366                /     CONSOLE TERMINAL AND/OR DEVICE 66 LINEPRINTER WITH LOGICAL CALLS TO
 8367                /     SPECIFIC LOCATIONS ON PAGE ZERO OF THE HIGHEST FIELD OF MEMORY.  THE P?S/8
 8368                /     MEMORY STATUS WORD PROVIDES ALL RELEVANT INFORMATION.  CALLS ARE PROVIDED
 8369                /     FOR CONSOLE INPUT, CONSOLE OUTPUT, LINEPRINTER OUTPUT AND LINEPRINTER
 8370                /     INPUT [USED ONLY FOR ACTIVE PARTICIPATION IN POTENTIAL FLOW-CONTROL
 8371                /     MECHANISMS].  A LOGICAL INTERRUPT HANDLER IS PROVIDED TO BE HOOKED INTO
 8372                /     ANY INTERRUPT-DRIVEN PROGRAM [AHEAD OF ANY PHYSICAL CONSOLE DEVICE
 8373                /     HANDLING].  THE P?S/8 IMPLEMENTATION OF FOCAL, 1969 USES THIS MECHANISM
 8374                /     FOR ALL RELEVANT INTERRUPT HANDLING.
 8375   
 8376                /     WHEN THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IS ENABLED, ALL SYSTEM DEVICE ERRORS ARE
 8377                /     REDIRECTED TO THE OVERLAY; THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER NO LONGER HALTS FOR
 8378                /     ERROR RECOVERY PURPOSES; INSTEAD, AN ERROR-HANDLING PORTION OF THE OVERLAY
 8379                /     IS USED TO ALERT THE USER TO ANY ERRORS WITH SEVERAL OPTIONS [RETRY, EXIT,
 8380                /     ETC.].  DEPENDING ON THE CONFIGURATION, VERBOSE ERROR MESSAGES CAN BE USED
 8381                /     SPECIFIC TO THE SYSTEM DEVICE HARDWARE.  FOR EXAMPLE, WHEN USED WITH THE
 8382                /     TC01/TC08 HANDLER, IT IS POSSIBLE TO GET EXPLICIT NOTICE OF SELECT,
 8383                /     TIMING, MARK, PARITY AND END ERRORS.
 8384   
 8385                /     CERTAIN SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLERS DEFINE ENHANCEMENTS TO BE CARRIED OUT BY
 8386                /     THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY.  FOR EXAMPLE, THE TC01/TC08 HANDLER USES A
 8387                /     COMMON VALUE FOR THE LAST BLOCK TRANSFERRED; THIS IS USED TO DETERMINE THE
 8388                /     BEST INITIAL SEARCH DIRECTION BASED ON LAST KNOWN BLOCK TRANSFER.
 8389                /     HOWEVER, IF THE SYSTEM DEVICE UNIT IS CHANGED, THIS CAN CAUSE AN
 8390                /     OCCASIONAL WRONG GUESS [INSTANTLY CORRECTED ONCE REALIZED TO BE IN ERROR].
 8391                /     THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY WILL ENHANCE THE DEVICE HANDLER TO USE A TABLE
 8392                /     OF LAST TRANSFERRED BLOCKS, ONE FOR EACH LOGICAL DRIVE UNIT TOTALLY
 8393                /     PREVENTING THIS MINOR PROBLEM.
 8394   
 8395                /     THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY CAN BE CONFIGURED TO SUPPORT A VARIETY OF
 8396                /     PHYSICAL ALTERNATE CONSOLE DEVICES SUCH AS THE VT8E AS AN EMULATED
 8397                /     TERMINAL, OR THE VR12/VR14 DISPLAY ON THE PDP-12.  DEVICES SIMILAR TO THE
 8398                /     DEFAULT CONSOLE CAN ALSO BE SUPPORTED SUCH AS A TERMINAL CONNECTED TO A
 8399                /     DEVICE 10/11 PT08 OR KL8JA OR OTHER INTERFACE. ALTERNATE PRINTING DEVICES
 8400                /     ARE ALSO SUPPORTED SUCH AS THE LS-120 SERIAL PRINTER WHICH REQUIRES
 8401                /     REVERSE CHANNEL FLOW CONTROL.
 8402   
 8403                /     SINCE THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY ONLY INTERFACES WITH COMPLIANT PROGRAMS
 8404                /     AND THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER, IT IS AVAILABLE FROM THE SHELL ENVIRONMENT
 8405                /     AS WELL AS THE BASIC P?S/8 SYSTEM.


