 8469                / 14) PS/8
 8470   
 8471                /     PS/8 IS THE ORIGINAL MARKETING NAME GIVEN TO A QUICK AND DIRTY OPERATING
 8472                /     SYSTEM HACKED UP OVER A WEEKEND BY RICHARD LARY.
 8473   
 8474                /     THE ORIGINAL NAME OF THIS WORK WAS THE FIRST UPWARD COMPATIBLE KEYBOARD
 8475                /     EDITOR AND MONITOR [NOTE THE OBVIOUS ACRONYM].  [PLANNED BUT NEVER
 8476                /     IMPLEMENTED WAS A SECOND UPWARD COMPATIBLE KEYBOARD EDITOR AND MONITOR.]
 8477                /     THE INTERNALS OF THIS SYSTEM WERE NEVER FULLY VETTED LEADING TO MANY
 8478                /     LIMITATIONS CRITICIZED BY MANY PEOPLE, MOST NOTABLY CHARLES LASNER, CHIEF
 8479                /     ARCHITECT OF THE P?S/8 PROJECT. [NOTE: CHARLES WAS RECRUITED TO WORK ON
 8480                /     THIS SYSTEM BUT DECLINED IN FAVOR OF IMPROVING THE R-L MONITOR.  HE IS
 8481                /     ALSO THE AUTHOR OF KERMIT-12 FOR OS/8 AND HAS HAD THE DUBIOUS DISTINCTION
 8482                /     OF WRITING ADDITIONAL UTILITIES FOR OS/8 TO SUPPORT THE KERMIT PROJECT.]
 8483   
 8484                /     BY THE TIME MANAGERIAL DECISION WAS MADE TO MARKET IT [AS PS/8] THE DESIGN
 8485                /     BECAME STAGNATED WITH LITTLE ABILITY TO IMPROVE; HALF-FINISHED FEATURES
 8486                /     THAT DON'T FUNCTION PROPERLY ABOUND AND WILL REMAIN SO INDEFINITELY.
 8487                /     [NOTE: THE MOST NOTABLE LIMITATION IS A SEGMENTED DIRECTORY THAT WOULD
 8488                /     SUGGEST THE ABILITY TO ADJUST THE OVERALL DIRECTORY SIZE; HOWEVER, IN NOW
 8489                /     STAGNATED IMPLEMENTATION, THERE IS NO PRACTICAL ABILITY TO EITHER LENGTHEN
 8490                /     OR SHORTEN THE DIRECTORY.  AS SUCH, THE RESULT IS A WORST CASE OUTCOME; ON
 8491                /     SMALL DEVICES THE DIRECTORY IS GENERALLY TOO LONG.  ON LARGER DEVICES, IT
 8492                /     IS ALL TOO EASY TO RUN OUT OF DIRECTORY ENTRY SPACE LONG BEFORE THE
 8493                /     UNDERLYING STORAGE IS COMPLETELY USED.  THE SEGMENTATION MERELY
 8494                /     CONTRIBUTES TO THIS PROBLEM AS A POINTLESS SOURCE OF OVERHEAD THAT
 8495                /     REQUIRES ADDITIONAL PROGRAMMING TO ACCESS.]
 8496   
 8497                /     AT THE REQUEST OF A DEC SALESMAN, THE NAME WAS CHANGED TO OS/8 BECAUSE HE
 8498                /     FELT IT WAS DIFFICULT TO SELL CUSTOMERS ON A "PROGRAMMING" SYSTEM AS
 8499                /     OPPOSED TO AN "OPERATING" SYSTEM.


