 8655   
 8656                / 18) JIM ROTH
 8657   
 8658                /     THE LATE JIM ROTH WAS RESPONSIBLE FOR MANY PROGRAMMING GEMS THROUGHOUT
 8659                /     P?S/8.  HE WROTE THE ORIGINAL RAW IMPLEMENTATION OF THE P?S/8 "PAL"
 8660                /     ASSEMBLER.  THIS WORK IS A FAST, CLEAN IMPLEMENTATION OF A REPLACEMENT
 8661                /     ASSEMBLER FOR DEC'S PAL III ASSEMBLER, WHICH WAS A VERY OLD AND POORLY
 8662                /     CODED PROGRAM ALBEIT WITH A MODICUM OF GOOD DESIGN POINTS; HOWEVER, PAL
 8663                /     III IS NOT ADAPTABLE TO ADDING ON ANY ADDITIONAL FEATURES.  JIM'S CODE IS
 8664                /     QUITE ELEGANT MAKING IT A RELATIVELY STRAIGHT-FORWARD [BUT LENGTHY] TASK
 8665                /     TO ADD ON ALL THE ADDITIONAL FEATURES A FULL-FLEDGED PDP-8 ASSEMBLER
 8666                /     REQUIRES.  [NOTE: THE REST OF THE ASSEMBLER WAS WRITTEN BY CHARLES LASNER
 8667                /     OVER A COURSE OF YEARS.  ADDED FEATURES INCLUDE DUAL MODE LINC ASSEMBLY
 8668                /     OPTIONS, LITERAL PROCESSING, QUIRKY SYNTAX SUPPORT [SUCH AS "JMP."],
 8669                /     MISCELLANEOUS ASSEMBLER DIRECTIVES AND CROSS-REFERENCE DUMP.]
 8670   
 8671                /     JIM WAS ALSO FASCINATED WITH RICHARD LARY'S "SLURP" LOADER AND WAS ABLE TO
 8672                /     CREATE A WORKING VERSION FOR THE DF32 MINIDISK AS PART OF A COMPLETE
 8673                /     ALTERNATIVE VERSION OF THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM FOR THE DF32.
 8674   
 8675                /     ALONG THE WAY HE INTENSELY STUDIED THE OPERATION OF THE TC01 CONTROLLER
 8676                /     AND IS THE AUTHOR OF MOST OF THE SOMEWHAT CONFUSING SEARCH AND MODE-CHANGE
 8677                /     CODE WITHIN THE TC01/TC08 SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER, INCLUDING THE INITIAL
 8678                /     SEARCH GUESS ROUTINE.  AS A DIRECT RESULT OF HIS SIGNIFICANTLY LOWERING
 8679                /     THE OVERALL CODE SPACE USED BY THE HANDLER, ENOUGH NEW SPACE WAS OBTAINED
 8680                /     TO ENVISION THE IMBEDDED SYSTEM LOADER THAT IS ARGUABLY THE SINGLE MOST
 8681                /     IMPORTANT CONTRIBUTION OF P?S/8 OVER THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM AT THE KERNEL
 8682                /     LEVEL.
 8683   
 8684                /     WHILE AN EMPLOYEE AT DEC, JIM WROTE THE QUICKSORT ROUTINES FOR
 8685                /     REORGANIZING THE SYMBOL TABLE FOR PRINTOUT WITHIN PAL8.  HE IS ALSO
 8686                /     RESPONSIBLE FOR EXTENSIVE REWRITE OF CERTAIN SPECIALIZED VERSIONS OF OS/8
 8687                /     [INDUSTRIAL] BASIC.  JIM ALSO REMOVED AN ENTIRE PAGE OF CODE SPACE WITHIN
 8688                /     POLY SPACEWAR BY USING A MORE ADVANCED TABLE LOOKUP METHOD FOR CALCULATING
 8689                /     VARIOUS TRIGONOMETRIC FUNCTIONS.  AS A RESULT, MANY MORE SPECIAL EFFECTS
 8690                /     AND OTHER FRILLS BECAME POSSIBLE WHILE STILL RUNNING AS A LEGITIMATE USER
